          "es": "Option text consists of a three-digit option ID and a one-digit action flag. The length of this field must be zero or a multiple of four. When this field is empty, all options will be set to their default values. The following options are supported: 020 = Append the 3DES Master File Key name to all responses. The value “MFK0” will be included when a 3DES Master File Key is not present in the HSM. By default the 3DES MFK name is not appended to the response. 021 = Append the detailed error code to error responses. By default, the detailed error code is not appended to the response. 023 = Remove the Carriage Return and Line Feed characters from all responses. By default, they are appended to the response. 027 = Use the rightmost 4 PIN digits for Diebold PIN verification. By default, the leftmost 4 PIN digits are used. 044 = Record invalid commands and error responses in the system log. This option has a significant performance impact . By default, the HSM does not record invalid command and error responses. When this option is enabled, warning messages may appear in the system log for certain commands the SCA sends to the HSM. This is not an error condition. The following action Flags are supported: D = Disable option E = Enable option",
