    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 109 - Confirm Security Policy\n\n- **Command ID:** `109`\n- **Title:** Confirm Security Policy\n- **PDF Pages:** 674 - 675\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 109 implements the security policy you defined with command 108. NOTE: This command is deprecated. Use the SCA HSM Configuration Management feature to configure the HSM security policy.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<109#[Warning Acknowledgment]#Challenge Response#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<209#Security Policy#Sequence Number#Serial Number#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier 3 |  | 109 |\n| 1 | [Warning 8 Acknowledgment] |  | If the security policy, defined in the 108 command, disabled both the sequence number and serial number validation, options (6E) and (6F), a warning message “SECURITY PRECAUTION: Are you sure?” was included in the 208 response. You must supply the following warning acknowledgment message: I accept before the HSM’s security policy will be implemented. This field is not case sensitive. This field is empty if the HSM’s security policy does not disable both of these options. |\n| 2 | Challenge Response 32, 36 |  | The result of encrypting or MACing the left and right challenge numbers returned in the response to command 108. If the 3DES MFK was used, this field will be the 32- character result of encrypting the challenges under variant 30 of the MFK. If the AES MFK was used, this field will be the concatenation of two MACs. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier 3 |  | 209 |\n| 1 | Security Policy Variable |  | The security policy that was just implemented. If the security policy is defined by several command 108 commands, this field will only show the security policy for the most recent 108 command. You can use the HSM Configuration Status (Command 9A) to obtain a complete list of commands and options enabled and disabled in the HSM. |\n| 2 | Sequence Number 16 |  | The number of times the security policy has been successfully updated. This value is used in processing of the security policy. It is displayed so you can keep track of the number of times each of your HSM’s security policy has been updated. Legal Characters: 0-9 |\n| 3 | HSM Serial Number 6 |  | The HSM serial number. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-Z |\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **NOTE:** This command is deprecated. Use the SCA HSM Configuration Management feature to configure the HSM security policy.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<109##203A98A64C8F900C62E1E8368E43A751#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<209#30=e;90=e;32=e;37=e;(66)=”e”;(A0)=”6”;10=d;30=d;98=d;(65)=d#0000000000000001#A7PV87#>\n```\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 109 - Confirm Security Policy\n\n- **Command ID:** `109`\n- **Title:** Confirm Security Policy\n- **PDF Pages:** 674 - 675\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 109 implements the security policy you defined with command 108. NOTE: This command is deprecated. Use the SCA HSM Configuration Management feature to configure the HSM security policy.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<109#[Warning Acknowledgment]#Challenge Response#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<209#Security Policy#Sequence Number#Serial Number#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier 3 |  | 109 |\n| 1 | [Warning 8 Acknowledgment] |  | If the security policy, defined in the 108 command, disabled both the sequence number and serial number validation, options (6E) and (6F), a warning message “SECURITY PRECAUTION: Are you sure?” was included in the 208 response. You must supply the following warning acknowledgment message: I accept before the HSM’s security policy will be implemented. This field is not case sensitive. This field is empty if the HSM’s security policy does not disable both of these options. |\n| 2 | Challenge Response 32, 36 |  | The result of encrypting or MACing the left and right challenge numbers returned in the response to command 108. If the 3DES MFK was used, this field will be the 32- character result of encrypting the challenges under variant 30 of the MFK. If the AES MFK was used, this field will be the concatenation of two MACs. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier 3 |  | 209 |\n| 1 | Security Policy Variable |  | The security policy that was just implemented. If the security policy is defined by several command 108 commands, this field will only show the security policy for the most recent 108 command. You can use the HSM Configuration Status (Command 9A) to obtain a complete list of commands and options enabled and disabled in the HSM. |\n| 2 | Sequence Number 16 |  | The number of times the security policy has been successfully updated. This value is used in processing of the security policy. It is displayed so you can keep track of the number of times each of your HSM’s security policy has been updated. Legal Characters: 0-9 |\n| 3 | HSM Serial Number 6 |  | The HSM serial number. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-Z |\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **NOTE:** This command is deprecated. Use the SCA HSM Configuration Management feature to configure the HSM security policy.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<109##203A98A64C8F900C62E1E8368E43A751#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<209#30=e;90=e;32=e;37=e;(66)=”e”;(A0)=”6”;10=d;30=d;98=d;(65)=d#0000000000000001#A7PV87#>\n```\n\n"
    },
