    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 1105 - Install a License in all Domains\n\n- **Command ID:** `1105`\n- **Title:** Install a License in all Domains\n- **PDF Pages:** 1334 - 1335\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 1105 simultaneously license in field scalability features, customer-specific commands and options for all domains that are currently configured. NOTE: After sending the command 1105 to the HSM, use the SCA to enable the customer-specific commands and options in each of the Domains. This command must be sent to Domain0.\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1105#Serial Number#License#MAC#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2105#Status#Version#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier 4 |  | 1105 |\n| 1 | HSM Serial Number 6 |  | The HSM serial number. |\n| 2 | License Variable |  | The encrypted form of the license. This field contains hexadecimal characters. The length of this field is divisible by 16. |\n| 3 | MAC 9 |  | The MAC of the serial number and license. This field contains 4 hexadecimal characters a space and 4 hexadecimal characters. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier 4 |  | 2105 |\n| 1 | Status 9, 11, 12 |  | COMPLETED = the command was successfully processed. MAC MISMATCH = the MAC did not validate. CONF INVALID = the decrypted license contained an error. SN MISMATCH = the HSM serial number does not match the serial number in the command. |\n| 2 | Version 4 |  | This field contains 4 hexadecimal characters, which are the command version. |\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **NOTE:** After sending the command 1105 to the HSM, use the SCA to enable the customer-specific commands and options in each of the Domains. This command must be sent to Domain0.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **NOTE:** This is not a valid example.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nThe serial number is 123456.\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1105#123456#E7F35DA354A09F32#B65F  3CA0#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2105#COMPLETED#VER1#>\n```\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 1105 - Install a License in all Domains\n\n- **Command ID:** `1105`\n- **Title:** Install a License in all Domains\n- **PDF Pages:** 1334 - 1335\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 1105 simultaneously license in field scalability features, customer-specific commands and options for all domains that are currently configured. NOTE: After sending the command 1105 to the HSM, use the SCA to enable the customer-specific commands and options in each of the Domains. This command must be sent to Domain0.\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1105#Serial Number#License#MAC#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2105#Status#Version#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier 4 |  | 1105 |\n| 1 | HSM Serial Number 6 |  | The HSM serial number. |\n| 2 | License Variable |  | The encrypted form of the license. This field contains hexadecimal characters. The length of this field is divisible by 16. |\n| 3 | MAC 9 |  | The MAC of the serial number and license. This field contains 4 hexadecimal characters a space and 4 hexadecimal characters. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier 4 |  | 2105 |\n| 1 | Status 9, 11, 12 |  | COMPLETED = the command was successfully processed. MAC MISMATCH = the MAC did not validate. CONF INVALID = the decrypted license contained an error. SN MISMATCH = the HSM serial number does not match the serial number in the command. |\n| 2 | Version 4 |  | This field contains 4 hexadecimal characters, which are the command version. |\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **NOTE:** After sending the command 1105 to the HSM, use the SCA to enable the customer-specific commands and options in each of the Domains. This command must be sent to Domain0.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **NOTE:** This is not a valid example.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nThe serial number is 123456.\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1105#123456#E7F35DA354A09F32#B65F  3CA0#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2105#COMPLETED#VER1#>\n```\n\n"
    },
