      "es": "# Command 1111 - HSM System Date and Time\n\n- **Command ID:** `1111`\n- **Title:** HSM System Date and Time\n- **PDF Pages:** 1337 - 1337\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 1111 returns the HSM’s system date and time.\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1111#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2111#YYMMDDHHMMSS#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1111 |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2111 |\n| 1 | YYMMDDHHMMSS | 1 | The two digit year, two digit month, two digit day, two digit hour, two digit minute, two digit second. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- By default, the time is Universal Coordinated Time (UTC). You can use the SCA HSM Time Adjustment feature to specify a local time.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1111#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2111#170525115300#>  (May 25,  2017  11:53:00)\n```\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 1111 - HSM System Date and Time\n\n- **Command ID:** `1111`\n- **Title:** HSM System Date and Time\n- **PDF Pages:** 1337 - 1337\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 1111 returns the HSM’s system date and time.\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1111#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2111#YYMMDDHHMMSS#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1111 |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2111 |\n| 1 | YYMMDDHHMMSS | 1 | The two digit year, two digit month, two digit day, two digit hour, two digit minute, two digit second. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- By default, the time is Universal Coordinated Time (UTC). You can use the SCA HSM Time Adjustment feature to specify a local time.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1111#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2111#170525115300#>  (May 25,  2017  11:53:00)\n```\n\n"
