      "es": "# Command 1120 - HSM System Information\n\n- **Command ID:** `1120`\n- **Title:** HSM System Information\n- **PDF Pages:** 1340 - 1340\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 1120 returns the HSM serial number, product ID, system software information, and Ax160 compatible personality version.\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1120#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2120#HSM Serial Number#Product ID#Loader Version#Personality Version#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier 4 |  | 1120 |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier 4 |  | 2120 |\n| 1 | HSM Serial Number Variable |  | This field contains the HSM’s alphanumeric serial number. |\n| 2 | Product ID Variable |  | This field contains the HSM product ID. |\n| 3 | Loader Version Variable |  | The loader software version. |\n| 4 | Personality Version Variable |  | The Ax160 personality version used as a base to create this version. For example a value of AKB2.30 indicates that Ax160 AKB version 2.30 was the base to create this Atalla HSM AT1000 version. |\n\n### Examples\n\nExamples\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1120#>\n```\n\n```\n<2120#SerialNumber=FXA19L#ProductID=AT1000#LoaderVersion=Loader  Version  1.22,Nov  20 2018  18:08:27#PersonalityVersion=Axx160 2.3X#>\n```\n\n```\n<2120#SerialNumber=FXA19L#ProductID=AT1000#LoaderVersion=Loader  Version  1.22,Nov  20 2018  18:08:27#PersonalityVersion=Axx160 2.3X#>\n```\n\n```\n<2120#SerialNumber=FXA19L#ProductID=AT1000#LoaderVersion=Loader  Version  1.22,Nov  20 2018  18:08:27#PersonalityVersion=Axx160 2.3X#>\n```\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 1120 - HSM System Information\n\n- **Command ID:** `1120`\n- **Title:** HSM System Information\n- **PDF Pages:** 1340 - 1340\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 1120 returns the HSM serial number, product ID, system software information, and Ax160 compatible personality version.\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1120#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2120#HSM Serial Number#Product ID#Loader Version#Personality Version#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier 4 |  | 1120 |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier 4 |  | 2120 |\n| 1 | HSM Serial Number Variable |  | This field contains the HSM’s alphanumeric serial number. |\n| 2 | Product ID Variable |  | This field contains the HSM product ID. |\n| 3 | Loader Version Variable |  | The loader software version. |\n| 4 | Personality Version Variable |  | The Ax160 personality version used as a base to create this version. For example a value of AKB2.30 indicates that Ax160 AKB version 2.30 was the base to create this Atalla HSM AT1000 version. |\n\n### Examples\n\nExamples\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1120#>\n```\n\n```\n<2120#SerialNumber=FXA19L#ProductID=AT1000#LoaderVersion=Loader  Version  1.22,Nov  20 2018  18:08:27#PersonalityVersion=Axx160 2.3X#>\n```\n\n```\n<2120#SerialNumber=FXA19L#ProductID=AT1000#LoaderVersion=Loader  Version  1.22,Nov  20 2018  18:08:27#PersonalityVersion=Axx160 2.3X#>\n```\n\n```\n<2120#SerialNumber=FXA19L#ProductID=AT1000#LoaderVersion=Loader  Version  1.22,Nov  20 2018  18:08:27#PersonalityVersion=Axx160 2.3X#>\n```\n\n"
