          "es": "This field must be empty when field 7 contains the number zero. When field 7 contains a value in the range of 1 through 99, this field must contain the optional block data. A maximum of 3912 characters can be provided in this field. Refer to Table 11 of ANSI X9 TR-31: Interoperable Secure Key Exchange Key Block Specification, April 15, 2018 for more information on these optional block identifiers. Each optional block has tag, length, and value (TLV) encoding. The tag is a two character ASCII identifier that indicates the content of the optional block. The length is the total length of the TLV value (2 bytes for tag + 2 bytes for length + length of data). The value is hexadecimal-ASCII variable-length data. This command does not separate the optional block data into different fields. You must concatenate all the data blocks, including any necessary padding blocks. The HSM will check that the number of blocks and lengths are well- formed and that the total length is a multiple of 8. If the length of the optional block data is not a multiple of the 3DES block size, the HSM will add a padding block PB. The HSM will return an error if the block already contains a PB block and the input is not a multiple of the block size. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII",
