    "source": "Utimaco Atalla AT1000 Command Reference Manual v8.60 (Command 1200)",
    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 1200 - HSM Compliance Information\n\n- **Command ID:** `1200`\n- **Title:** HSM Compliance Information\n- **PDF Pages:** 1341 - 1342\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 1200 returns the necessary information to confirm PCI-HSM or FIPS 140-3 compliance.\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1200#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2200#Certificate#Digital Signature#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1200 |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2200 |\n| 1 | Personality Version Loader Version PSMCU Version CMS-OCT Version [CMS-NTX Version] Chassis Version ACS Hardware Part Number | Variable Variable Variable Variable Variable Variable Variable | This line returns the HSM and Personality version along with the date the personality was implemented. This line is needed for both PCI-HSM and FIPS140-3 validation. This line returns the Loader Version along with the implementation date. This line is needed for FIPS140-3 validation. This line returns the PSMCU version and the implementation date. This line is needed for FIPS140-3 validation. This line returns the CMS-OCT version and the implementation date. This line is needed for FIPS140-3 validation. This line gives the CMS-NTX version and the implementation date. This line is needed for FIPS140-3 validation. This line will not be present when the Nitrox chip is not present. This line returns the server chassis version. This line is needed for PCI-HSM validation. This line returns the ACS Hardware part number. This line is needed for FIPS140-3 validation. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- The response data consists of a single field, with individual version numbers separated into separate lines for human readability. These lines are described separately below.\n\n### Examples\n\nExamples\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1200#>\n```\n\n```\n<2200#Atalla HSM  AT1000-AKB  Version:  8.60.0.0,  Date: Jul  15  2024,  Time: 16:24:41Loader Version  1.22,  Nov  20  2018  18:08:27PSMCU Version  1.0.0,  Nov  4  2019  15:27:48CMS-OCT  Version  1.0.0,  Oct 25  2019  13:08:19CMS-NTX  Version  1.0.0,  Oct 25  2019  13:08:17Hardware  Chassis  HW-AT-HSM-V1ACS  Adapter:  C9B60-2108A#>\n```\n\n```\n<2200#Atalla HSM AT1000-VAR Version: 8.60.0.0, Date: Jul 15 2024, Time: 16:25:37Loader Version 1.22, Nov 20 2018 18:08:27PSMCU Version 1.0.0, Nov  4 2019 15:27:48CMS-OCT Version 1.0.0, Oct 25 2019 13:08:19CMS-NTX Version 1.0.0, Oct 25 2019 13:08:17Hardware Chassis HW-AT-HSM-V1ACS Adapter: C9B60-2108A#>\n```\n\n```\n<2200#Atalla HSM AT1000-AKB PCI-HSM Version: 8.60.0.0, Date: Jul 15 2024, Time: 16:26:40Loader Version 1.22, Nov 20 2018 18:08:27PSMCU Version 1.0.0, Nov  4 2019 15:27:48CMS-OCT Version 1.0.0, Oct 25 2019 13:08:19CMS-NTX Version 1.0.0, Oct 25 2019 13:08:17Hardware Chassis HW-AT-HSM-V1ACS Adapter: C9B60-2108A#>\n```\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 1200 - HSM Compliance Information\n\n- **Command ID:** `1200`\n- **Title:** HSM Compliance Information\n- **PDF Pages:** 1341 - 1342\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 1200 returns the necessary information to confirm PCI-HSM or FIPS 140-3 compliance.\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1200#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2200#Certificate#Digital Signature#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1200 |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2200 |\n| 1 | Personality Version Loader Version PSMCU Version CMS-OCT Version [CMS-NTX Version] Chassis Version ACS Hardware Part Number | Variable Variable Variable Variable Variable Variable Variable | This line returns the HSM and Personality version along with the date the personality was implemented. This line is needed for both PCI-HSM and FIPS140-3 validation. This line returns the Loader Version along with the implementation date. This line is needed for FIPS140-3 validation. This line returns the PSMCU version and the implementation date. This line is needed for FIPS140-3 validation. This line returns the CMS-OCT version and the implementation date. This line is needed for FIPS140-3 validation. This line gives the CMS-NTX version and the implementation date. This line is needed for FIPS140-3 validation. This line will not be present when the Nitrox chip is not present. This line returns the server chassis version. This line is needed for PCI-HSM validation. This line returns the ACS Hardware part number. This line is needed for FIPS140-3 validation. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- The response data consists of a single field, with individual version numbers separated into separate lines for human readability. These lines are described separately below.\n\n### Examples\n\nExamples\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1200#>\n```\n\n```\n<2200#Atalla HSM  AT1000-AKB  Version:  8.60.0.0,  Date: Jul  15  2024,  Time: 16:24:41Loader Version  1.22,  Nov  20  2018  18:08:27PSMCU Version  1.0.0,  Nov  4  2019  15:27:48CMS-OCT  Version  1.0.0,  Oct 25  2019  13:08:19CMS-NTX  Version  1.0.0,  Oct 25  2019  13:08:17Hardware  Chassis  HW-AT-HSM-V1ACS  Adapter:  C9B60-2108A#>\n```\n\n```\n<2200#Atalla HSM AT1000-VAR Version: 8.60.0.0, Date: Jul 15 2024, Time: 16:25:37Loader Version 1.22, Nov 20 2018 18:08:27PSMCU Version 1.0.0, Nov  4 2019 15:27:48CMS-OCT Version 1.0.0, Oct 25 2019 13:08:19CMS-NTX Version 1.0.0, Oct 25 2019 13:08:17Hardware Chassis HW-AT-HSM-V1ACS Adapter: C9B60-2108A#>\n```\n\n```\n<2200#Atalla HSM AT1000-AKB PCI-HSM Version: 8.60.0.0, Date: Jul 15 2024, Time: 16:26:40Loader Version 1.22, Nov 20 2018 18:08:27PSMCU Version 1.0.0, Nov  4 2019 15:27:48CMS-OCT Version 1.0.0, Oct 25 2019 13:08:19CMS-NTX Version 1.0.0, Oct 25 2019 13:08:17Hardware Chassis HW-AT-HSM-V1ACS Adapter: C9B60-2108A#>\n```\n\n"
    },
