      "es": "# Command 1204 - HSM Log Signing Key Certificate\n\n- **Command ID:** `1204`\n- **Title:** HSM Log Signing Key Certificate\n- **PDF Pages:** 1343 - 1344\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 1204 returns the certificate of the Log Signing Key which signs the signed.log file when the HSM is operating in PCI-HSM mode. The public key contained in this certificate is used to verify the signature appended each record of the log file. NOTE: This command is only available when the HSM is operating in PCI-HSM mode.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1204#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2204#Certificate#Digital Signature#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **NOTE:** This command is only available when the HSM is operating in PCI-HSM mode.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1204#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2204###>\n```\n\n",
