      "es": "# Command 1216 - HSM Battery Status\n\n- **Command ID:** `1216`\n- **Title:** HSM Battery Status\n- **PDF Pages:** 1347 - 1348\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 1216 returns the status of the HSM batteries. The HSM includes non-rechargeable batteries that power the Atalla Cryptographic System’s physical security components only when the HSM is not connected to an AC power source. The batteries are rated to last the life of the HSM, under normal operating conditions they do not require maintenance.\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1216#1#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2216#1#Status#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1216 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | This field contains the number 1. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2216 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | This field contains the contents of command field 1. |\n| 2 | Status | 4, 7, 8 | The battery status, where: GOOD = the battery capacity is in the normal range. REPLACE = the batteries should be replaced, the HSM will not zeroize if disconnected from AC power. CRITICAL = the batteries must be replaced immediately, the HSM may zeroize if disconnected from AC power. EXPIRED = the HSM will zeroize if disconnected from AC power. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- To schedule a battery replacement, contact Atalla technical support or your local service representative.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1216#1#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2216#1#GOOD#>\n```\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 1216 - HSM Battery Status\n\n- **Command ID:** `1216`\n- **Title:** HSM Battery Status\n- **PDF Pages:** 1347 - 1348\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 1216 returns the status of the HSM batteries. The HSM includes non-rechargeable batteries that power the Atalla Cryptographic System’s physical security components only when the HSM is not connected to an AC power source. The batteries are rated to last the life of the HSM, under normal operating conditions they do not require maintenance.\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1216#1#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2216#1#Status#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1216 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | This field contains the number 1. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2216 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | This field contains the contents of command field 1. |\n| 2 | Status | 4, 7, 8 | The battery status, where: GOOD = the battery capacity is in the normal range. REPLACE = the batteries should be replaced, the HSM will not zeroize if disconnected from AC power. CRITICAL = the batteries must be replaced immediately, the HSM may zeroize if disconnected from AC power. EXPIRED = the HSM will zeroize if disconnected from AC power. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- To schedule a battery replacement, contact Atalla technical support or your local service representative.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1216#1#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2216#1#GOOD#>\n```\n\n"
