      "es": "# Command 122 - Generate RSA-AKB for Root Public Key\n\n- **Command ID:** `122`\n- **Title:** Generate RSA-AKB for Root Public Key\n- **PDF Pages:** 733 - 735\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 122 generates an RSA-AKB for the root public key. Reference Information: Section 9, “Asymmetric Cryptography.”\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Disabled | 3DES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<122#Public Exponent#Modulus#Hash32#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<222#Public Key#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier 3 |  | 122 |\n| 1 | Public Exponent Variable |  | The Public Key’s public exponent. The value of the public exponent must be odd, cannot be 01, and must be less than the value of the modulus. This field contains hexadecimal characters. |\n| 2 | Modulus Variable |  | The Public Key’s modulus. This field contains hexadecimal characters. |\n| 3 | Hash32 1 - 3 |  | The Hash-32 encrypted under variant 30 of the MFK. Hash-32 is the leftmost 32 hexadecimal characters of the SHA1 hash result of the public key. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier 2 |  | 222 |\n| 1 | Public Key Variable |  | The Public Key in RSA-AKB format. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- The HSM will return an error if the value of the public exponent is even or 01.\n- When the HSM is operating in PCI-HSM mode and contains a 3key-3DES MFK, the maximum size of the RSA key is 2048 bits.\n- When the HSM is operating in PCI-HSM mode and contains a 2key-3DES MFK, the maximum size of the RSA key is 1024 bits.\n- Use Command 126 to generate the SHA-1 hash of the public key. When generating the public key hash, the public key must be provided in the following format: public exponent length|public exponent|modulus length|modulus\n- The RSA-AKB header value will be 1SRVN000.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **NOTE:** This command is deprecated, new applications should use command 12A.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nPublic exponent: 010001\n\nModulus:\n\n```\n<126#0#3#0#263###>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<226#0#8F6D7481A85C02DAEAAAA11F4CFF3F3A245F6CA9#>\n```\n\nHash-32 -The leftmost 32 characters of the hash returned in field 2 of the response.\n\nEmfk.30(Hash-32): 5B747FD2E5F8C8FC11443A86474466AF\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<122#010001##5B747FD2E5F8C8FC11443A86474466AF#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<222#1SRVN000,,B4B87296C77F55E9#>\n```\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 122 - Generate RSA-AKB for Root Public Key\n\n- **Command ID:** `122`\n- **Title:** Generate RSA-AKB for Root Public Key\n- **PDF Pages:** 733 - 735\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 122 generates an RSA-AKB for the root public key. Reference Information: Section 9, “Asymmetric Cryptography.”\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Disabled | 3DES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<122#Public Exponent#Modulus#Hash32#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<222#Public Key#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier 3 |  | 122 |\n| 1 | Public Exponent Variable |  | The Public Key’s public exponent. The value of the public exponent must be odd, cannot be 01, and must be less than the value of the modulus. This field contains hexadecimal characters. |\n| 2 | Modulus Variable |  | The Public Key’s modulus. This field contains hexadecimal characters. |\n| 3 | Hash32 1 - 3 |  | The Hash-32 encrypted under variant 30 of the MFK. Hash-32 is the leftmost 32 hexadecimal characters of the SHA1 hash result of the public key. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier 2 |  | 222 |\n| 1 | Public Key Variable |  | The Public Key in RSA-AKB format. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- The HSM will return an error if the value of the public exponent is even or 01.\n- When the HSM is operating in PCI-HSM mode and contains a 3key-3DES MFK, the maximum size of the RSA key is 2048 bits.\n- When the HSM is operating in PCI-HSM mode and contains a 2key-3DES MFK, the maximum size of the RSA key is 1024 bits.\n- Use Command 126 to generate the SHA-1 hash of the public key. When generating the public key hash, the public key must be provided in the following format: public exponent length|public exponent|modulus length|modulus\n- The RSA-AKB header value will be 1SRVN000.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **NOTE:** This command is deprecated, new applications should use command 12A.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nPublic exponent: 010001\n\nModulus:\n\n```\n<126#0#3#0#263###>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<226#0#8F6D7481A85C02DAEAAAA11F4CFF3F3A245F6CA9#>\n```\n\nHash-32 -The leftmost 32 characters of the hash returned in field 2 of the response.\n\nEmfk.30(Hash-32): 5B747FD2E5F8C8FC11443A86474466AF\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<122#010001##5B747FD2E5F8C8FC11443A86474466AF#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<222#1SRVN000,,B4B87296C77F55E9#>\n```\n\n"
