      "es": "# Command 1225 - HSM MAC Addresses\n\n- **Command ID:** `1225`\n- **Title:** HSM MAC Addresses\n- **PDF Pages:** 1356 - 1357\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 1225 returns the MAC addresses for NIC1, NIC2, NIC3 and NIC4. It can also include information on NIC bonding.\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1225#[Mode#]>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2225#NIC1 MAC Address#NIC2 MAC Address#[NIC3 MAC Address#] Printing MAC Address#[Bonding NIC1/NIC3#Bonding NIC2/NIC4#]>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1225 |\n| 1 | [Mode#] | 0,1 | This field is optional. If set to one, the command returns the address for all configured NICs, and information on NIC bonding. If this field is absent, the command returns response fields 0, 1, 2, and 4. Legal Characters: 1 |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2225 |\n| 1 | NIC1 MAC address | 17 | This field contains the NIC1 MAC address xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx format. |\n| 2 | NIC2 MAC address | 17 | This field contains the NIC2 MAC address xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx format. |\n| 3 | [NIC3 MAC address#] | 0, 17 | When command field 1 contains a 1, this field contains the NIC3 MAC address xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx format. Otherwise this field is not present in the response. |\n| 4 | Printing MAC address | 0, 17 | When command field 1 contains a 1, or if the config.prm file contains the keyword IPADDR_4, this field contains the NIC4 MAC address xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx format. Otherwise this field is empty. |\n| 5 | [Bonding NIC1/NIC3# | 0, 1 | This field is only present when command field 1 contains a 1, When present it indicates if bonding is enabled for NICs 1 and 3. Possible values are: Y = Bonding is enabled N = Bonding is not enabled |\n| 6 | Bonding NIC2/NIC4#] | 0,1 | This field is only present when command field 1 contains a 1, When present it indicates if bonding is enabled for NICs 2 and 4. Possible values are: Y = Bonding is enabled N = Bonding is not enabled |\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1225#>\n```\n\n```\n<2225#3c:ec:ef:73:3a:82#3c:ec:ef:73:3a:83#e4:3d:1a:30:61:47#>\n```\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1225#1#>\n```\n\n```\n<2225#3c:ec:ef:73:3a:82#3c:ec:ef:73:3a:83#e4:3d:1a:30:61:46#e4:3d:1a:30:61:47#Y#Y#>\n```\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 1225 - HSM MAC Addresses\n\n- **Command ID:** `1225`\n- **Title:** HSM MAC Addresses\n- **PDF Pages:** 1356 - 1357\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 1225 returns the MAC addresses for NIC1, NIC2, NIC3 and NIC4. It can also include information on NIC bonding.\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1225#[Mode#]>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2225#NIC1 MAC Address#NIC2 MAC Address#[NIC3 MAC Address#] Printing MAC Address#[Bonding NIC1/NIC3#Bonding NIC2/NIC4#]>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1225 |\n| 1 | [Mode#] | 0,1 | This field is optional. If set to one, the command returns the address for all configured NICs, and information on NIC bonding. If this field is absent, the command returns response fields 0, 1, 2, and 4. Legal Characters: 1 |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2225 |\n| 1 | NIC1 MAC address | 17 | This field contains the NIC1 MAC address xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx format. |\n| 2 | NIC2 MAC address | 17 | This field contains the NIC2 MAC address xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx format. |\n| 3 | [NIC3 MAC address#] | 0, 17 | When command field 1 contains a 1, this field contains the NIC3 MAC address xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx format. Otherwise this field is not present in the response. |\n| 4 | Printing MAC address | 0, 17 | When command field 1 contains a 1, or if the config.prm file contains the keyword IPADDR_4, this field contains the NIC4 MAC address xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx format. Otherwise this field is empty. |\n| 5 | [Bonding NIC1/NIC3# | 0, 1 | This field is only present when command field 1 contains a 1, When present it indicates if bonding is enabled for NICs 1 and 3. Possible values are: Y = Bonding is enabled N = Bonding is not enabled |\n| 6 | Bonding NIC2/NIC4#] | 0,1 | This field is only present when command field 1 contains a 1, When present it indicates if bonding is enabled for NICs 2 and 4. Possible values are: Y = Bonding is enabled N = Bonding is not enabled |\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1225#>\n```\n\n```\n<2225#3c:ec:ef:73:3a:82#3c:ec:ef:73:3a:83#e4:3d:1a:30:61:47#>\n```\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1225#1#>\n```\n\n```\n<2225#3c:ec:ef:73:3a:82#3c:ec:ef:73:3a:83#e4:3d:1a:30:61:46#e4:3d:1a:30:61:47#Y#Y#>\n```\n\n"
