    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 1227 - Reset HSM to Factory State\n\n- **Command ID:** `1227`\n- **Title:** Reset HSM to Factory State\n- **PDF Pages:** 1360 - 1361\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 1227 and 1228 operate as a pair, they reset the HSM to the factory state, erasing the user-defined security policy, and all user-defined keys. The default security policy is restored. NOTE: This command is only allowed on the serial port.\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1227#RESET_TO_FACTORY_STATE#[MODE#]>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2227#nnnnnn#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1227 |\n| 1 | RESET_TO_FACTORY_ STATE | 23 | Must be uppercase characters. |\n| 2 | [MODE#] | 0, 5 | This field is optional. When present, it contains the word CLEAR, which instructs the HSM to clear the security audit log. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2227 |\n| 1 | nnnnnn | 6 | The random challenge number. This field contains six hexadecimal characters, which are supplied as field 1 in command 1228. |\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **NOTE:** This command is only allowed on the serial port.\n\n### Examples\n\nExamples\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1227#RESET_TO_FACTORY_STATE#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2227#7B390C#>\n```\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1227#RESET_TO_FACTORY_STATE#CLEAR#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2227#44D0EA#>\n```\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 1227 - Reset HSM to Factory State\n\n- **Command ID:** `1227`\n- **Title:** Reset HSM to Factory State\n- **PDF Pages:** 1360 - 1361\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 1227 and 1228 operate as a pair, they reset the HSM to the factory state, erasing the user-defined security policy, and all user-defined keys. The default security policy is restored. NOTE: This command is only allowed on the serial port.\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1227#RESET_TO_FACTORY_STATE#[MODE#]>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2227#nnnnnn#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1227 |\n| 1 | RESET_TO_FACTORY_ STATE | 23 | Must be uppercase characters. |\n| 2 | [MODE#] | 0, 5 | This field is optional. When present, it contains the word CLEAR, which instructs the HSM to clear the security audit log. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2227 |\n| 1 | nnnnnn | 6 | The random challenge number. This field contains six hexadecimal characters, which are supplied as field 1 in command 1228. |\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **NOTE:** This command is only allowed on the serial port.\n\n### Examples\n\nExamples\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1227#RESET_TO_FACTORY_STATE#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2227#7B390C#>\n```\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1227#RESET_TO_FACTORY_STATE#CLEAR#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2227#44D0EA#>\n```\n\n"
    },
