    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 1228 - Confirm Reset HSM to Factory State\n\n- **Command ID:** `1228`\n- **Title:** Confirm Reset HSM to Factory State\n- **PDF Pages:** 1362 - 1362\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 1228 confirms the HSM’s reset to factory state. Prior to using this command, you must first use command 1227 to generate the input for field 1. NOTE: This command is only allowed on the serial port.\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1228#nnnnnn#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2228#Status#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1228 |\n| 1 | nnnnnn | n | This field contains the random challenge number returned as field 1 of response to command 1227. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2228 |\n| 1 | Status | 2, 16 | This field contains the status result, where: ok = the HSM has been reset to factory state Bad Confirmation = the wrong value was entered in command field 1, and the HSM has not been reset to factory state. You must send command 1227 again to generate a new challenge value, and then send command 1228 again. |\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **NOTE:** This command is only allowed on the serial port.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1228#nnnnnn#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2228#ok#>\n```\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 1228 - Confirm Reset HSM to Factory State\n\n- **Command ID:** `1228`\n- **Title:** Confirm Reset HSM to Factory State\n- **PDF Pages:** 1362 - 1362\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 1228 confirms the HSM’s reset to factory state. Prior to using this command, you must first use command 1227 to generate the input for field 1. NOTE: This command is only allowed on the serial port.\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1228#nnnnnn#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2228#Status#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1228 |\n| 1 | nnnnnn | n | This field contains the random challenge number returned as field 1 of response to command 1227. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2228 |\n| 1 | Status | 2, 16 | This field contains the status result, where: ok = the HSM has been reset to factory state Bad Confirmation = the wrong value was entered in command field 1, and the HSM has not been reset to factory state. You must send command 1227 again to generate a new challenge value, and then send command 1228 again. |\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **NOTE:** This command is only allowed on the serial port.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1228#nnnnnn#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2228#ok#>\n```\n\n"
    },
