        "es": "[NOTE] ECDSA keys cannot use the key slots. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII or 0-199 Response description Field Contents Length Description 0 Response identifier 2 224 1 0 1 This field contains the decimal digit zero (0). Legal Characters: zero (0) 2 Signature Variable The generated signature. For RSA signatures, the length of this field is twice the size of the modulus. For ECDSA signatures, this field contains the values R and S concatenated together. R and S may be left padded with zeros, if necessary, so that both are the same length. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F Response description (Continued) Field Contents Length Description 3 [Check Digits#] [8] The value of this field is based on the first digit of the header of the private key: Version 1 AKBs = field contains the leftmost eight hexadecimal characters of the SHA-1 hash of the RSA private key. Version 3 AKBs = field contains the leftmost eight hexadecimal characters of the SHA-256 hash of the RSA public key. This field is present only when command field 7 contains a value in the range of 0-199. This field is present only when command field 7 contains a value in the range 0-199. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F",
