    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 128 - Change AKB Header\n\n- **Command ID:** `128`\n- **Title:** Change AKB Header\n- **PDF Pages:** 771 - 773\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 128 provides the ability to change an AKB header as permitted in X9.143, for 3DES, AES, HMAC, RSA, and ECC keys. This command cannot be used to move from a version 1 to a version 3 AKB. Reference Information: Section 2, “Key types and management methods.”\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<128#Key#New Header#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<228#Updated AKB#[Check Digits#]>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 3 | 128 |\n| 1 | Key | Variable | The AKB of the key to be changed. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n| 2 | New Header | 8 | The header to be applied to the key in field 1. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 228 |\n| 1 | Updated AKB | Variable | The AKB of the key with the new AKB header applied. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n| 2 | Check Digits | 6, 8, 10, 14 | Working key check digits: AES - are the leftmost ten hexadecimal characters from the CMAC of all zeros. 3DES - are the leftmost six hexadecimal characters from encrypting all zeros. HMAC - the leftmost 14 hexadecimal characters of the SHA-256 hash of the KMAC. RSA (V1) - the leftmost eight hexadecimal characters of the SHA-1 hash of the private key. RSA (V3) - the leftmost eight hexadecimal characters of the SHA-256 hash of the public key. ECC - the leftmost 8 hexadecimal characters of the SHA- 256 hash of the public key. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- The HSM supports the following approved in X9.143 changes:\n- An exportable key may become non-exportable. For example, the AKB Header Byte 4-Exportability values ‘E’ or ‘S’ may become ‘N’.\n- A key that supports both encrypt and decrypt can become either encrypt-only or decrypt-only. For\n\n### Examples\n\nexample, the AKB Header Byte 3-Mode of Use value of ‘N’ can become ‘E’ or ‘D’.\n\nA key that supports both generate and verify can become generate-only or verify-only. For example, the\n\nA Key Exchange Key (AKB header byte 1 = ‘K’) or an ATM Master Key (AKB header byte 1 ‘A’) can be\n\nA KEK that imports only a single type of key (byte 6 = I or K) can be converted to a TR-31 KBPK if option\n\nWhen option EE is enabled, the AKB length of the Key (field 1) may be 110 characters.\n\nWhen option EE is enabled, an AES or HMAC Key supplied in Key (field 1), and returned in response\n\nClear text Data Key: 0123456789ABCDEF FEDCBA9876543210\n\nNew AKB Header: 1DDEN000\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<128#1DDNE000,4509C24B1C13C379F1EC519B255CD9B96F777E7BBDCC5D47,8998D7F464EED3A2#1DDEN000#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<228#1DDEN000,773E58C18135F60CAB2362B4328262777F42600DD3DCCC9B,CD1DA78E43DF394F#08D7B4#>\n```\n\nClear text Data Key: 0123456789ABCDEF FEDCBA9876543210\n\nNew AKB Header: 3DDEN000\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<128#3DDNE000,3CD5FA8CAFEC255765F47D21CF2054A4DBE3D4702BA92314,13367F249EC81204#3DDEN000#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<228#3DDEN000,BD0FC7BA8FA3D480F264D405051592A321D6D5135926D147,0CC3B66AE58AACDB#08D7B4#>\n```\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 128 - Change AKB Header\n\n- **Command ID:** `128`\n- **Title:** Change AKB Header\n- **PDF Pages:** 771 - 773\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 128 provides the ability to change an AKB header as permitted in X9.143, for 3DES, AES, HMAC, RSA, and ECC keys. This command cannot be used to move from a version 1 to a version 3 AKB. Reference Information: Section 2, “Key types and management methods.”\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<128#Key#New Header#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<228#Updated AKB#[Check Digits#]>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 3 | 128 |\n| 1 | Key | Variable | The AKB of the key to be changed. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n| 2 | New Header | 8 | The header to be applied to the key in field 1. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 228 |\n| 1 | Updated AKB | Variable | The AKB of the key with the new AKB header applied. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n| 2 | Check Digits | 6, 8, 10, 14 | Working key check digits: AES - are the leftmost ten hexadecimal characters from the CMAC of all zeros. 3DES - are the leftmost six hexadecimal characters from encrypting all zeros. HMAC - the leftmost 14 hexadecimal characters of the SHA-256 hash of the KMAC. RSA (V1) - the leftmost eight hexadecimal characters of the SHA-1 hash of the private key. RSA (V3) - the leftmost eight hexadecimal characters of the SHA-256 hash of the public key. ECC - the leftmost 8 hexadecimal characters of the SHA- 256 hash of the public key. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- The HSM supports the following approved in X9.143 changes:\n- An exportable key may become non-exportable. For example, the AKB Header Byte 4-Exportability values ‘E’ or ‘S’ may become ‘N’.\n- A key that supports both encrypt and decrypt can become either encrypt-only or decrypt-only. For\n\n### Examples\n\nexample, the AKB Header Byte 3-Mode of Use value of ‘N’ can become ‘E’ or ‘D’.\n\nA key that supports both generate and verify can become generate-only or verify-only. For example, the\n\nA Key Exchange Key (AKB header byte 1 = ‘K’) or an ATM Master Key (AKB header byte 1 ‘A’) can be\n\nA KEK that imports only a single type of key (byte 6 = I or K) can be converted to a TR-31 KBPK if option\n\nWhen option EE is enabled, the AKB length of the Key (field 1) may be 110 characters.\n\nWhen option EE is enabled, an AES or HMAC Key supplied in Key (field 1), and returned in response\n\nClear text Data Key: 0123456789ABCDEF FEDCBA9876543210\n\nNew AKB Header: 1DDEN000\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<128#1DDNE000,4509C24B1C13C379F1EC519B255CD9B96F777E7BBDCC5D47,8998D7F464EED3A2#1DDEN000#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<228#1DDEN000,773E58C18135F60CAB2362B4328262777F42600DD3DCCC9B,CD1DA78E43DF394F#08D7B4#>\n```\n\nClear text Data Key: 0123456789ABCDEF FEDCBA9876543210\n\nNew AKB Header: 3DDEN000\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<128#3DDNE000,3CD5FA8CAFEC255765F47D21CF2054A4DBE3D4702BA92314,13367F249EC81204#3DDEN000#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<228#3DDEN000,BD0FC7BA8FA3D480F264D405051592A321D6D5135926D147,0CC3B66AE58AACDB#08D7B4#>\n```\n\n"
    },
