      "es": "# Command 12C - Verify or Delete RSA Key Table Entry\n\n- **Command ID:** `12C`\n- **Title:** Verify or Delete RSA Key Table Entry\n- **PDF Pages:** 794 - 795\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 12C verifies or deletes an RSA key stored in the RSA key table. Reference Information: Section 9, “Asymmetric Cryptography.”\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Disabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<12C#Operation#Key Slot#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<22C#Remaining Key Slots#[Check Digits#]>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 3 | 12C |\n| 1 | Operation | 6, 7 | The operation to be performed. This field contains either VERIFY or DELETE. |\n| 2 | Key Slot | 1, 3 | The slot in the RSA Key Table that will be verified or deleted. This field contains a decimal number in the range of 0- 199. When field 1 = DELETE, this field may contain the word ALL, which means that all the keys in the RSA Key Table will be deleted. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 22C |\n| 1 | Remaining Key Slots | Variable | The number of empty key slots. |\n| 2 | [Check Digits#] | [8, 18] | The value of this field is based on the first digit of the header of the RSA key: 1 = field contains the leftmost eight hexadecimal characters of the SHA-1 hash of the RSA key. 3 = field contains the leftmost eight hexadecimal characters of the SHA-256 hash of the public key. This field is present only when command field 1 = VERIFY. When the key slot is empty, this field contains the text string NO KEY IN KEY SLOT. |\n\n### Examples\n\nExamples\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<12C#VERIFY#1#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<22C#198#8F6D7481#>\n```\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<12C#DELETE#7#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<22C#199#>\n```\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<12C#VERIFY#7#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<22C#199#NO  KEY  IN  KEY  SLOT#>\n```\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<12C#DELETE#ALL#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<22C#200#>\n```\n\n",
