              "en": "The AKB of the Key Exchange Key which encrypts the components of the Private Key. This key must be either a 2key- or 3key-3DES key, or an AES key. The Key Exchange Key determines which RSA headers can be exported. KEK Header Allowed RSA Header 1pRX*000, 1pRGE000 or 3pRGE000 3pRX*000, where * = E or N. 3KDE*000 Any valid RSA private key header with 3KDN*00f, exportability ‘S’ where * = E, N, or S. 3KJE*00N, Any valid RSA header private key header with 3KJN*00f, exportability ‘S’ where * = E, N, or S. If option E8 is enabled, the KEK must be at least as strong as the RSA key. This means: KEK Maximum RSA key size 2key-3DES 1024 bits 3key-3DES 2048 bits AES128 3072 bits AES192 or AES256 4096 bits (HSM limit) Legal Characters: Printable ASCII"
