    "source": "Utimaco Atalla AT1000 Command Reference Manual v8.60 (Response 1351)",
    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 1351 - HSM Domain System Information\n\n- **Command ID:** `1351`\n- **Title:** HSM Domain System Information\n- **PDF Pages:** 1368 - 1370\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 1351 returns the name and Master File Key check digits (MFKCDx) for each defined domain. If the domain has not been defined, the entire field for that domain will be empty. Domain0 will always be present. If multiple domain support is not enabled, only information for Domain0 will be returned. NOTE: This command is only allowed on the serial port. It should only be sent to an HSM that is configured for multiple Domains.\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1351#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2351#VNSP0=NAME0(MFKCD0)#[VNSP1=NAME1(MFKCD1)]#[VNSP2=NAME2(MFKCD2)]# [VNSP3=NAME3(MFKCD3)]#[VNSP4=NAME4(MFKCD4)]#[VNSP5=NAME5(MFKCD5)]# [VNSP6=NAME6(MFKCD6)]#[VNSP7=NAME7(MFKCD7)]#[VNSP8=NAME8(MFKCD8)]# [VNSP9=NAME9(MFKCD9)]#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1351 |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2351 |\n| 1 | VNSP0=NAME0 (MFKCD0) | Variable | The name and (3DES MFK check digits) for Domain0. |\n| 2 | [VNSP1=NAME0 (MFKCD1)] | 0, Variable | The name and (3DES MFK check digits) for Domain1. This field is empty if VNSP1 has not been defined in the config.prm file. |\n| 3 | [VNSP2=NAME0 (MFKCD2)] | 0, Variable | The name and (3DES MFK check digits) for Domain2. This field is empty if VNSP1 has not been defined in the config.prm file. |\n| 4 | [VNSP3=NAME0 (MFKCD3)] | 0, Variable | The name and (3DES MFK check digits) for Domain3. This field is empty if VNSP1 has not been defined in the config.prm file. |\n| 5 | [VNSP4=NAME0 (MFKCD4)] | 0, Variable | The name and (3DES MFK check digits) for Domain4. This field is empty if VNSP1 has not been defined in the config.prm file. |\n| 6 | [VNSP5=NAME0 (MFKCD5)] | 0, Variable | The name and (3DES MFK check digits) for Domain5. This field is empty if VNSP1 has not been defined in the config.prm file. |\n| 7 | [VNSP6=NAME0 (MFKCD6)] | 0, Variable | The name and (3DES MFK check digits) for Domain6. This field is empty if VNSP1 has not been defined in the config.prm file. |\n| 8 | [VNSP7=NAME0 (MFKCD7)] | 0, Variable | The name and (3DES MFK check digits) for Domain7. This field is empty if VNSP1 has not been defined in the config.prm file. |\n| 9 | [VNSP8=NAME0 (MFKCD8)] | 0, Variable | The name and (3DES MFK check digits) for Domain8. This field is empty if VNSP1 has not been defined in the config.prm file. |\n| 10 | [VNSP9=NAME0 (MFKCD9)] | 0, Variable | The name and (3DES MFK check digits) for Domain9. This field is empty if VNSP1 has not been defined in the config.prm file. |\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **NOTE:** This command is only allowed on the serial port. It should only be sent to an HSM that is configured for multiple Domains.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nVNSP0 Name and 3DES MFK check digits: PROD (B196)\n\nVNSP9 Name and 3DES MFK check digits: DEV (57AC)\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1351#>\n```\n\n```\n<2351#VNSP0=PROD(B196)#VNSP1=UAT(057A)#VNSP2=(1234)###VNSP5=TEST5()####VNSP9=DEV(57AC)#>\n```\n\n```\n<2351#VNSP0=(B196)##########>\n```\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 1351 - HSM Domain System Information\n\n- **Command ID:** `1351`\n- **Title:** HSM Domain System Information\n- **PDF Pages:** 1368 - 1370\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 1351 returns the name and Master File Key check digits (MFKCDx) for each defined domain. If the domain has not been defined, the entire field for that domain will be empty. Domain0 will always be present. If multiple domain support is not enabled, only information for Domain0 will be returned. NOTE: This command is only allowed on the serial port. It should only be sent to an HSM that is configured for multiple Domains.\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1351#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2351#VNSP0=NAME0(MFKCD0)#[VNSP1=NAME1(MFKCD1)]#[VNSP2=NAME2(MFKCD2)]# [VNSP3=NAME3(MFKCD3)]#[VNSP4=NAME4(MFKCD4)]#[VNSP5=NAME5(MFKCD5)]# [VNSP6=NAME6(MFKCD6)]#[VNSP7=NAME7(MFKCD7)]#[VNSP8=NAME8(MFKCD8)]# [VNSP9=NAME9(MFKCD9)]#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1351 |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2351 |\n| 1 | VNSP0=NAME0 (MFKCD0) | Variable | The name and (3DES MFK check digits) for Domain0. |\n| 2 | [VNSP1=NAME0 (MFKCD1)] | 0, Variable | The name and (3DES MFK check digits) for Domain1. This field is empty if VNSP1 has not been defined in the config.prm file. |\n| 3 | [VNSP2=NAME0 (MFKCD2)] | 0, Variable | The name and (3DES MFK check digits) for Domain2. This field is empty if VNSP1 has not been defined in the config.prm file. |\n| 4 | [VNSP3=NAME0 (MFKCD3)] | 0, Variable | The name and (3DES MFK check digits) for Domain3. This field is empty if VNSP1 has not been defined in the config.prm file. |\n| 5 | [VNSP4=NAME0 (MFKCD4)] | 0, Variable | The name and (3DES MFK check digits) for Domain4. This field is empty if VNSP1 has not been defined in the config.prm file. |\n| 6 | [VNSP5=NAME0 (MFKCD5)] | 0, Variable | The name and (3DES MFK check digits) for Domain5. This field is empty if VNSP1 has not been defined in the config.prm file. |\n| 7 | [VNSP6=NAME0 (MFKCD6)] | 0, Variable | The name and (3DES MFK check digits) for Domain6. This field is empty if VNSP1 has not been defined in the config.prm file. |\n| 8 | [VNSP7=NAME0 (MFKCD7)] | 0, Variable | The name and (3DES MFK check digits) for Domain7. This field is empty if VNSP1 has not been defined in the config.prm file. |\n| 9 | [VNSP8=NAME0 (MFKCD8)] | 0, Variable | The name and (3DES MFK check digits) for Domain8. This field is empty if VNSP1 has not been defined in the config.prm file. |\n| 10 | [VNSP9=NAME0 (MFKCD9)] | 0, Variable | The name and (3DES MFK check digits) for Domain9. This field is empty if VNSP1 has not been defined in the config.prm file. |\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **NOTE:** This command is only allowed on the serial port. It should only be sent to an HSM that is configured for multiple Domains.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nVNSP0 Name and 3DES MFK check digits: PROD (B196)\n\nVNSP9 Name and 3DES MFK check digits: DEV (57AC)\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1351#>\n```\n\n```\n<2351#VNSP0=PROD(B196)#VNSP1=UAT(057A)#VNSP2=(1234)###VNSP5=TEST5()####VNSP9=DEV(57AC)#>\n```\n\n```\n<2351#VNSP0=(B196)##########>\n```\n\n"
    },
