    "source": "Utimaco Atalla AT1000 Command Reference Manual v8.60 (Command 14)",
    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 14 - Load ATM Master Key, Diebold\n\n- **Command ID:** `14`\n- **Title:** Load ATM Master Key, Diebold\n- **PDF Pages:** 148 - 149\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 14 encrypts the ATM Master Key under an Encryption Key for downloading to Diebold ATMs.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<14#1#Variants#Master Key#Encryption Key#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<24#1#Master Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 14 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Variants | 2 | The MFK variants. This field contains two variant values. The first variant value defines the type of Master Key which can be downloaded to the ATM. The second variant value defines the type of Encryption Key which is currently present in the ATM. The following types of Mater Keys and their corresponding variants can be downloaded. MAC Master Key = 1 PIN Master Key = 5 Visa Master Key = 5 The following types of Encryption Keys and their corresponding variants can exist in the ATMs: Communications Key = 1 ATMA Key = 5 PIN Master Key-1 = 5 Visa Master Key-1 = 5 |\n| 3 | Master Key | 16, 32 | The ATM Master Key encrypted under the proper variant of the MFK. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n| 4 | Encryption Key | 16, 32 | The cryptogram of the key under which the ATM Master Key is to be encrypted. This Encryption Key is encrypted under the proper variant of the MFK. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 24 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Master Key | 16, 32 | The Master Key encrypted under the Encryption Key. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters. |\n| 3 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The Master Key check digits are the leftmost four hexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros under the Master Key. If option 88 is enabled, the leftmost six check digits are returned. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- Manually load the ATM with its initial keys.\n- Generate the appropriate Encryption Key for encrypting the ATM Master Key and encrypt it using the proper variant of the MFK. The Encryption Key length must be equal or greater than the length of the ATM Master Key, it cannot be a replicated single-length key.\n- Generate the ATM Master Key, it cannot be a replicated single-length key.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nVariant: 1\n\nVariant: 5\n\nClear-text Master Key: 3333 3333 3333 3333 5555 6666 7777 8888\n\nClear-text Encryption Key: 1111 1111 1111 1111 0123 4567 89AB CDEF\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<14#1#15#321992E944B0F4231DE1CF689E9699D6#118A17BA953BD16C608FC3DDBDDA3E56#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<24#1#CA652727D7ECC3FF29D072B935BEC86E#B15B#>\n```\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 14 - Load ATM Master Key, Diebold\n\n- **Command ID:** `14`\n- **Title:** Load ATM Master Key, Diebold\n- **PDF Pages:** 148 - 149\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 14 encrypts the ATM Master Key under an Encryption Key for downloading to Diebold ATMs.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<14#1#Variants#Master Key#Encryption Key#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<24#1#Master Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 14 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Variants | 2 | The MFK variants. This field contains two variant values. The first variant value defines the type of Master Key which can be downloaded to the ATM. The second variant value defines the type of Encryption Key which is currently present in the ATM. The following types of Mater Keys and their corresponding variants can be downloaded. MAC Master Key = 1 PIN Master Key = 5 Visa Master Key = 5 The following types of Encryption Keys and their corresponding variants can exist in the ATMs: Communications Key = 1 ATMA Key = 5 PIN Master Key-1 = 5 Visa Master Key-1 = 5 |\n| 3 | Master Key | 16, 32 | The ATM Master Key encrypted under the proper variant of the MFK. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n| 4 | Encryption Key | 16, 32 | The cryptogram of the key under which the ATM Master Key is to be encrypted. This Encryption Key is encrypted under the proper variant of the MFK. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 24 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Master Key | 16, 32 | The Master Key encrypted under the Encryption Key. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters. |\n| 3 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The Master Key check digits are the leftmost four hexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros under the Master Key. If option 88 is enabled, the leftmost six check digits are returned. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- Manually load the ATM with its initial keys.\n- Generate the appropriate Encryption Key for encrypting the ATM Master Key and encrypt it using the proper variant of the MFK. The Encryption Key length must be equal or greater than the length of the ATM Master Key, it cannot be a replicated single-length key.\n- Generate the ATM Master Key, it cannot be a replicated single-length key.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nVariant: 1\n\nVariant: 5\n\nClear-text Master Key: 3333 3333 3333 3333 5555 6666 7777 8888\n\nClear-text Encryption Key: 1111 1111 1111 1111 0123 4567 89AB CDEF\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<14#1#15#321992E944B0F4231DE1CF689E9699D6#118A17BA953BD16C608FC3DDBDDA3E56#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<24#1#CA652727D7ECC3FF29D072B935BEC86E#B15B#>\n```\n\n"
    },
