    "source": "Utimaco Atalla AT1000 Command Reference Manual v8.60 (Command 143)",
    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 143 - Import non-PTS Public Key\n\n- **Command ID:** `143`\n- **Title:** Import non-PTS Public Key\n- **PDF Pages:** 877 - 879\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 143 allows a MAC to be put on an RSA or ECC key that is used for non-PIN related activities. CAUTION: There is no dual control over this command, so any user of the HSM can introduce a public key. Keys loaded this way can never be used to encrypt PIN keys or key wrapping keys that can protect PIN keys, because PIN keys and the keys that protect them must always be under dual control.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Disabled | AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<143#Header#Public Exponent/Curve#Modulus/Public Key x coordinate# [Public key y coordinate]#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<243#Public Key#Check digits#>\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier 3 |  | 143 |\n| 1 | Header 8 |  | The AKB header to be applied to the public key. Headers Supported: RSA keys: 3KREN00N, 3sRVN000, 3pRVN000, 3DREN000. ECDSA keys: 3seVN000, 3peVN000. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n| 2 | Public exponent Variable or Curve |  | RSA keys (AKB header byte 2 = R), the public key’s public exponent. The value of the public exponent must be odd, it cannot be 01 and it must be less than the value of the modulus. ECC keys (AKB header byte 2 = e), the constant indicating the named curve. Supported Values: Curve Constant NIST P-521 2B81040023 NIST P-256 2A8648CE3D030107 Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n| 3 | RSA Modulus Variable or ECC public key x coordinate |  | RSA keys, the public key’s modulus. If this value starts with 00, the 00 is not included in the AKB. The maximum size of the RSA modulus is 4096 bits (ignoring leading zeros). The minimum size is 1024 bits. This command ignores option 8F. ECC keys, the x coordinate of the public key (Qx). Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n| 4 | [Public key y Variable coordinate] |  | RSA keys, this field must be empty. ECC keys, the y coordinate of the public key (Qy). EMV EC-SDSA keys, this field may be empty. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier 3 |  | 243 |\n| 1 | Public Key Variable |  | The public key, in AKB format, version 3. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n| 2 | Check digits 8 |  | The first 8 digits from the SHA-256 hash of the public key. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> **CAUTION:** There is no dual control over this command, so any user of the HSM can introduce a public key. Keys loaded this way can never be used to encrypt PIN keys or key wrapping keys that can protect PIN keys, because PIN keys and the keys that protect them must always be under dual control.\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 143 - Import non-PTS Public Key\n\n- **Command ID:** `143`\n- **Title:** Import non-PTS Public Key\n- **PDF Pages:** 877 - 879\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 143 allows a MAC to be put on an RSA or ECC key that is used for non-PIN related activities. CAUTION: There is no dual control over this command, so any user of the HSM can introduce a public key. Keys loaded this way can never be used to encrypt PIN keys or key wrapping keys that can protect PIN keys, because PIN keys and the keys that protect them must always be under dual control.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Disabled | AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<143#Header#Public Exponent/Curve#Modulus/Public Key x coordinate# [Public key y coordinate]#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<243#Public Key#Check digits#>\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier 3 |  | 143 |\n| 1 | Header 8 |  | The AKB header to be applied to the public key. Headers Supported: RSA keys: 3KREN00N, 3sRVN000, 3pRVN000, 3DREN000. ECDSA keys: 3seVN000, 3peVN000. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n| 2 | Public exponent Variable or Curve |  | RSA keys (AKB header byte 2 = R), the public key’s public exponent. The value of the public exponent must be odd, it cannot be 01 and it must be less than the value of the modulus. ECC keys (AKB header byte 2 = e), the constant indicating the named curve. Supported Values: Curve Constant NIST P-521 2B81040023 NIST P-256 2A8648CE3D030107 Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n| 3 | RSA Modulus Variable or ECC public key x coordinate |  | RSA keys, the public key’s modulus. If this value starts with 00, the 00 is not included in the AKB. The maximum size of the RSA modulus is 4096 bits (ignoring leading zeros). The minimum size is 1024 bits. This command ignores option 8F. ECC keys, the x coordinate of the public key (Qx). Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n| 4 | [Public key y Variable coordinate] |  | RSA keys, this field must be empty. ECC keys, the y coordinate of the public key (Qy). EMV EC-SDSA keys, this field may be empty. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier 3 |  | 243 |\n| 1 | Public Key Variable |  | The public key, in AKB format, version 3. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n| 2 | Check digits 8 |  | The first 8 digits from the SHA-256 hash of the public key. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> **CAUTION:** There is no dual control over this command, so any user of the HSM can introduce a public key. Keys loaded this way can never be used to encrypt PIN keys or key wrapping keys that can protect PIN keys, because PIN keys and the keys that protect them must always be under dual control.\n\n"
    },
