    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 15 - Change ATM Communications Key, Diebold\n\n- **Command ID:** `15`\n- **Title:** Change ATM Communications Key, Diebold\n- **PDF Pages:** 158 - 159\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 15 encrypts a Communications Key for downloading to a Diebold ATM.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Disabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<15#1#Variant#Communications Key#Encryption Key#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<25#1#Communications Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 15 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Variant | 1 | The MFK variant under which the Encryption Key was encrypted. This field contains a number, either 1 or 5. |\n| 3 | Communications Key | 16, 32 | The Communications Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n| 4 | Encryption Key | 16, 32 | The Encryption Key encrypted under the variant 1 or 5 of the MFK. This key encrypts the Communications Key. If the variant specified in field 2 is 1, the old Communications Key encrypts the Communications Key supplied in field 3. If the variant specified in field 2 is 5, the PIN Master Key encrypts the Communications Key supplied in field 3. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 25 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Communications Key | 16, 32 | The Communications Key encrypted under the Encryption Key. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters. |\n| 3 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The Communications Key check digits are the leftmost four hexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros under the Communications Key. If option 88 is enabled, the leftmost six check digits are returned. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- The Communications Key in a Diebold ATM encrypts PINs; therefore, although the term communications key is used for this key, it is supported in the Atalla key management scheme as a PIN Encryption Key.\n- Generate the Encryption Key which will encrypt the new Communications Key.\n- Generate the new Communications Key (KC). Variant Example The 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A. See “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n- Variant: 1\n- Clear-text new Communications Key: 0123456789ABCDEF 1111222233334444 The new Communications Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK: AE86D417E64E07E0 D538A881DE91EAF1\n- Clear-text Encryption Key (P):3333 3333 3333 3333 5555 6666 7777 8888 The Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK: 321992E944B0F423 1DE1CF689E9699D6 The command looks like this: <15#1#1#AE86D417E64E07E0D538A881DE91EAF1#321992E944B0F4231DE1CF689E9699D6#> The HSM returns this response: <25#1#4DEB22EE1652AA8A216FF8BA794E8AFD#4E15#>\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 15 - Change ATM Communications Key, Diebold\n\n- **Command ID:** `15`\n- **Title:** Change ATM Communications Key, Diebold\n- **PDF Pages:** 158 - 159\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 15 encrypts a Communications Key for downloading to a Diebold ATM.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Disabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<15#1#Variant#Communications Key#Encryption Key#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<25#1#Communications Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 15 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Variant | 1 | The MFK variant under which the Encryption Key was encrypted. This field contains a number, either 1 or 5. |\n| 3 | Communications Key | 16, 32 | The Communications Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n| 4 | Encryption Key | 16, 32 | The Encryption Key encrypted under the variant 1 or 5 of the MFK. This key encrypts the Communications Key. If the variant specified in field 2 is 1, the old Communications Key encrypts the Communications Key supplied in field 3. If the variant specified in field 2 is 5, the PIN Master Key encrypts the Communications Key supplied in field 3. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 25 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Communications Key | 16, 32 | The Communications Key encrypted under the Encryption Key. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters. |\n| 3 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The Communications Key check digits are the leftmost four hexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros under the Communications Key. If option 88 is enabled, the leftmost six check digits are returned. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- The Communications Key in a Diebold ATM encrypts PINs; therefore, although the term communications key is used for this key, it is supported in the Atalla key management scheme as a PIN Encryption Key.\n- Generate the Encryption Key which will encrypt the new Communications Key.\n- Generate the new Communications Key (KC). Variant Example The 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A. See “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n- Variant: 1\n- Clear-text new Communications Key: 0123456789ABCDEF 1111222233334444 The new Communications Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK: AE86D417E64E07E0 D538A881DE91EAF1\n- Clear-text Encryption Key (P):3333 3333 3333 3333 5555 6666 7777 8888 The Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK: 321992E944B0F423 1DE1CF689E9699D6 The command looks like this: <15#1#1#AE86D417E64E07E0D538A881DE91EAF1#321992E944B0F4231DE1CF689E9699D6#> The HSM returns this response: <25#1#4DEB22EE1652AA8A216FF8BA794E8AFD#4E15#>\n\n"
    },
