              "en": "The KEK encrypted under the MFK. After combining the 3DES key components into a key, the HSM uses the KEK to encrypt the 3DES key. This field must be empty if the components are from an AES key. (Byte 2 = 'J' in the component AKBs.) This field contains 74 printable ASCII characters. The KEK can be a 2key-3DES key, it can be a 3key-3DES key only if the MFK is also a 3key-3DES key. The length of the KEK must be equal to or greater than the length of the key components. Headers Supported: 3DES MFK 1KDE*000, 1KDN*000, where * = E or N. Headers Supported: AES MFK 3KDE*000, 3KDN*000, where * = E, N, or S."
