    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 16 - Encrypt Financial Institution Table, Diebold\n\n- **Command ID:** `16`\n- **Title:** Encrypt Financial Institution Table, Diebold\n- **PDF Pages:** 170 - 171\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 16 encrypts a Working Key to be downloaded to a Diebold ATM Financial Institution Table.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Disabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<16#1#Variant#Working Key#Exchange Key#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<26#1#Working Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 16 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Variant | 1 | The variant to be applied to the MFK when encrypting the Working Key. This field contains a decimal number, either 2 or 5. |\n| 3 | Working Key | 16 | The Working Key encrypted under variant 2 or 5 of the MFK. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n| 4 | Exchange Key | 16 | The Exchange Key encrypted under variant 5 of the MFK. This key encrypts the Working Key. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 26 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Communications Key | 16 | The Working Key encrypted under the Exchange Key. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters. |\n| 3 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The Working Key check digits are the leftmost four hexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros under the Working Key. If option 88 is enabled, the leftmost six check digits are returned. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- Each execution of this command encrypts a single key for a FIT entry.\n- Generate the Exchange Key.\n- All keys must be 1key-3DES keys. Variant Example The 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A. See “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n- Clear-text Working Key: 3333 3333 3333 3333 The Working Key encrypted under variant 2 of the MFK: C22F 5A1F 22D1 ABF1\n- Clear-text Exchange Key: 1111 1111 1111 1111 The Exchange Key encrypted under variant 5 of the MFK:118A 17BA 953B D16C The command looks like this: <16#1#2#C22F5A1F22D1ABF1#118A17BA953BD16C#> The HSM returns this response: <26#1#F679786E2411E3DE#ADC6#>\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 16 - Encrypt Financial Institution Table, Diebold\n\n- **Command ID:** `16`\n- **Title:** Encrypt Financial Institution Table, Diebold\n- **PDF Pages:** 170 - 171\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 16 encrypts a Working Key to be downloaded to a Diebold ATM Financial Institution Table.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Disabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<16#1#Variant#Working Key#Exchange Key#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<26#1#Working Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 16 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Variant | 1 | The variant to be applied to the MFK when encrypting the Working Key. This field contains a decimal number, either 2 or 5. |\n| 3 | Working Key | 16 | The Working Key encrypted under variant 2 or 5 of the MFK. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n| 4 | Exchange Key | 16 | The Exchange Key encrypted under variant 5 of the MFK. This key encrypts the Working Key. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 26 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Communications Key | 16 | The Working Key encrypted under the Exchange Key. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters. |\n| 3 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The Working Key check digits are the leftmost four hexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros under the Working Key. If option 88 is enabled, the leftmost six check digits are returned. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- Each execution of this command encrypts a single key for a FIT entry.\n- Generate the Exchange Key.\n- All keys must be 1key-3DES keys. Variant Example The 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A. See “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n- Clear-text Working Key: 3333 3333 3333 3333 The Working Key encrypted under variant 2 of the MFK: C22F 5A1F 22D1 ABF1\n- Clear-text Exchange Key: 1111 1111 1111 1111 The Exchange Key encrypted under variant 5 of the MFK:118A 17BA 953B D16C The command looks like this: <16#1#2#C22F5A1F22D1ABF1#118A17BA953BD16C#> The HSM returns this response: <26#1#F679786E2411E3DE#ADC6#>\n\n"
    },
