    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 16 - Encrypt Financial Institution Table, IBM 3624\n\n- **Command ID:** `16`\n- **Title:** Encrypt Financial Institution Table, IBM 3624\n- **PDF Pages:** 174 - 175\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 16 encrypts a PIN Verification Key to be downloaded to a IBM 3624 ATM Financial Institution Table.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Disabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<16#3#PIN Verification Key#ATM Master Key#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<26#3#PIN Verification Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 16 |\n| 1 | 3 | 1 | 3 = IBM 3624 |\n| 2 | PIN Verification Key | 16 | The PIN Verification Key encrypted under variant 5 of the MFK. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n| 3 | ATM Master Key | 16 | The ATM Master Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK. This key encrypts the PIN Verification Key. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 26 |\n| 1 | 3 | 1 | 3 = IBM 3624 |\n| 2 | PIN Verification Key | 16 | The PIN Verification Key encrypted under the ATM Master Key. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters. |\n| 3 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The PIN Verification Key check digits are the leftmost four hexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros under the PIN Verification Key. If option 88 is enabled, the leftmost six check digits are returned. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- Generate the PIN Verification Key.\n- Generate the ATM Master Key.\n- All keys must be 1key-3DES keys. Variant Example The 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A. See “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n- Clear-text PIN Verification Key: 2222 2222 2222 2222 The PIN Verification Key encrypted under variant 5 of the MFK: EA45 F59C 6242 F687\n- Clear-text ATM Master Key: 1111 1111 1111 1111 The ATM Master Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK: C628 3830 AE9E 875A The command looks like this: <16#3#EA45F59C6242F687#C6283830AE9E875A#> The HSM returns this response: <26#3#950973182317F80B#0096#>\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 16 - Encrypt Financial Institution Table, IBM 3624\n\n- **Command ID:** `16`\n- **Title:** Encrypt Financial Institution Table, IBM 3624\n- **PDF Pages:** 174 - 175\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 16 encrypts a PIN Verification Key to be downloaded to a IBM 3624 ATM Financial Institution Table.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Disabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<16#3#PIN Verification Key#ATM Master Key#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<26#3#PIN Verification Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 16 |\n| 1 | 3 | 1 | 3 = IBM 3624 |\n| 2 | PIN Verification Key | 16 | The PIN Verification Key encrypted under variant 5 of the MFK. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n| 3 | ATM Master Key | 16 | The ATM Master Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK. This key encrypts the PIN Verification Key. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 26 |\n| 1 | 3 | 1 | 3 = IBM 3624 |\n| 2 | PIN Verification Key | 16 | The PIN Verification Key encrypted under the ATM Master Key. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters. |\n| 3 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The PIN Verification Key check digits are the leftmost four hexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros under the PIN Verification Key. If option 88 is enabled, the leftmost six check digits are returned. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- Generate the PIN Verification Key.\n- Generate the ATM Master Key.\n- All keys must be 1key-3DES keys. Variant Example The 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A. See “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n- Clear-text PIN Verification Key: 2222 2222 2222 2222 The PIN Verification Key encrypted under variant 5 of the MFK: EA45 F59C 6242 F687\n- Clear-text ATM Master Key: 1111 1111 1111 1111 The ATM Master Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK: C628 3830 AE9E 875A The command looks like this: <16#3#EA45F59C6242F687#C6283830AE9E875A#> The HSM returns this response: <26#3#950973182317F80B#0096#>\n\n"
    },
