    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 179 - Generate EMV AES MAC\n\n- **Command ID:** `179`\n- **Title:** Generate EMV AES MAC\n- **PDF Pages:** 1005 - 1008\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 179 supports EMV issuer scripting. It generates a Message Authentication Code in accordance with EMV standards using AES-based derivation. Reference Information: Section 7, “Processing EMV and Visa stored value cards.”\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Disabled | AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<179#EMV Derivation Type#Issuer Master Key - MAC#Application PAN# [Application PAN Sequence Number]#Diversification Data#MAC Length# [Continuation IV]#Padded Data#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<279#MAC Length#MAC or Continuation IV#Session Key Check Digits# Issuer Master Key - MAC Check Digits#>\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 3 | 179 |\n| 1 | Derivation Type | 1 | This field determines what keys are used to generate the MAC and how they are derived. The following derivation type is supported: A = Method C and EMV common session from the EMV v4.3 Book 2. A session key of the same length as the Issuer Master Key is produced. Legal Characters: A |\n| 2 | Issuer Master Key - MAC | 74, 90, 106, 110 | The Issuer Master Key for Message Integrity. This key must be an AES 128, 192, or 256 bit key. Headers Supported: 3mJN*00M, where * = E, S, or N. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n| 3 | Application PAN | 1-20 | The Primary Account Number (PAN). Legal Characters: 0 - 9 |\n| 4 | [Application PAN Sequence Number] | 0, 2 | The optional application PAN Sequence Number. This field may contain a 2-digit decimal value. If this field is empty, the HSM will use a PAN Sequence Number of 00. Legal Characters: 0 - 9 |\n| 5 | Diversification Data | 16 | This field contains the Application Cryptogram. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n| 6 | MAC Length | 1 | The size of the MAC to be generated. Allowed values are: 0 = More data expected, no MAC verified. 1 = 64 bits Legal Characters: 0-1 |\n| 7 | [Continuation IV] | 0, 74, 110 | There are two use cases when this field must be empty: - When all of the data to be MACed is supplied in field 8. - When field 8 contains the first portion of the data to be MACed. The header for the continuation IV in response field 2 will be 1IJNE00c. command, this field should contain the continuation-IV from response field 2. Headers Supported: 3IJN*00c, where * = E, N, or S. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n| 8 | Padded Data | 16 - 3584 | The data used to calculate the MAC. Per the EMV specification, the data should be right-padded with a single byte (expressed as two hexadecimal characters \"80\"), followed by a variable number of binary zeros bytes (expressed as two hexadecimal characters \"00\") to make the total data length a multiple of 16 bytes (32 hexadecimal characters). The HSM does not enforce this data format; it only requires that the length of data is a multiple of 32 hexadecimal characters. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 3 | 278 |\n| 1 | MAC Length | 1 | This field contains the value of command field 6. Legal Characters: 0, 1 |\n| 2 | MAC or Continuation IV | 16 74, 110 | This field will contain the calculated MAC. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F If command field 6 is 0, then this field contains the continuation IV encrypted under the AES MFK using header supplied in command field 7. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n| 3 | Session Key check digits | 10 | The leftmost 10 digits of the CMAC of all zeros. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n| 4 | Issuer Master Key - MAC check digits | 10 | The leftmost 10 digits of the CMAC of all zeros. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 179 - Generate EMV AES MAC\n\n- **Command ID:** `179`\n- **Title:** Generate EMV AES MAC\n- **PDF Pages:** 1005 - 1008\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 179 supports EMV issuer scripting. It generates a Message Authentication Code in accordance with EMV standards using AES-based derivation. Reference Information: Section 7, “Processing EMV and Visa stored value cards.”\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Disabled | AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<179#EMV Derivation Type#Issuer Master Key - MAC#Application PAN# [Application PAN Sequence Number]#Diversification Data#MAC Length# [Continuation IV]#Padded Data#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<279#MAC Length#MAC or Continuation IV#Session Key Check Digits# Issuer Master Key - MAC Check Digits#>\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 3 | 179 |\n| 1 | Derivation Type | 1 | This field determines what keys are used to generate the MAC and how they are derived. The following derivation type is supported: A = Method C and EMV common session from the EMV v4.3 Book 2. A session key of the same length as the Issuer Master Key is produced. Legal Characters: A |\n| 2 | Issuer Master Key - MAC | 74, 90, 106, 110 | The Issuer Master Key for Message Integrity. This key must be an AES 128, 192, or 256 bit key. Headers Supported: 3mJN*00M, where * = E, S, or N. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n| 3 | Application PAN | 1-20 | The Primary Account Number (PAN). Legal Characters: 0 - 9 |\n| 4 | [Application PAN Sequence Number] | 0, 2 | The optional application PAN Sequence Number. This field may contain a 2-digit decimal value. If this field is empty, the HSM will use a PAN Sequence Number of 00. Legal Characters: 0 - 9 |\n| 5 | Diversification Data | 16 | This field contains the Application Cryptogram. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n| 6 | MAC Length | 1 | The size of the MAC to be generated. Allowed values are: 0 = More data expected, no MAC verified. 1 = 64 bits Legal Characters: 0-1 |\n| 7 | [Continuation IV] | 0, 74, 110 | There are two use cases when this field must be empty: - When all of the data to be MACed is supplied in field 8. - When field 8 contains the first portion of the data to be MACed. The header for the continuation IV in response field 2 will be 1IJNE00c. command, this field should contain the continuation-IV from response field 2. Headers Supported: 3IJN*00c, where * = E, N, or S. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n| 8 | Padded Data | 16 - 3584 | The data used to calculate the MAC. Per the EMV specification, the data should be right-padded with a single byte (expressed as two hexadecimal characters \"80\"), followed by a variable number of binary zeros bytes (expressed as two hexadecimal characters \"00\") to make the total data length a multiple of 16 bytes (32 hexadecimal characters). The HSM does not enforce this data format; it only requires that the length of data is a multiple of 32 hexadecimal characters. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 3 | 278 |\n| 1 | MAC Length | 1 | This field contains the value of command field 6. Legal Characters: 0, 1 |\n| 2 | MAC or Continuation IV | 16 74, 110 | This field will contain the calculated MAC. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F If command field 6 is 0, then this field contains the continuation IV encrypted under the AES MFK using header supplied in command field 7. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n| 3 | Session Key check digits | 10 | The leftmost 10 digits of the CMAC of all zeros. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n| 4 | Issuer Master Key - MAC check digits | 10 | The leftmost 10 digits of the CMAC of all zeros. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n\n"
    }
