    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 19 - Translate Working Key for Local Storage\n\n- **Command ID:** `19`\n- **Title:** Translate Working Key for Local Storage\n- **PDF Pages:** 178 - 179\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 19 translates a Working Key from Base Key encryption (without a variant) to MFK encryption for local storage and subsequent use. This command imports a Working Key from a network that does not use Atalla variants.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Disabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<19#Variant#Base Key#Working Key#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<29#Working Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 19 |\n| 1 | Variant | 1, 2 | The MFK variant which encrypts the Base Key.This field contains a decimal number in the range of 0 - 31. See “Variant” on page 59 for a list of supported variants. |\n| 2 | Base Key | 16, 32 | The Base Key encrypted under variant of the MFK specified in field 1. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n| 3 | Working Key | 16, 32 | The Working Key encrypted under the Base Key. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 29 |\n| 1 | Working Key | 16, 32 | The Working Key encrypted under the variant of the MFK specified in field 1 of the command. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters. |\n| 2 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The Working Key check digits are the leftmost four hexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros under the Working Key. If option 88 is enabled, the leftmost six check digits are returned. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- Option 65 must be enabled if command field 1 contains the number 0.\n- Encrypt the Base Key under the appropriate variant of the MFK. Variant Example The 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A. See “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n- Variant: 1\n- Clear-text Base Key: 0123 4567 89AB CDEF The Base Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK: AE86 D417 E64E 07E0\n- Clear-text PIN Encryption Key: FEDC BA98 7654 3210 The PIN encryption key encrypted under the Base Key: 12C6 26AF 058B 433B The command looks like this: <19#1#AE86D417E64E07E0#12C626AF058B433B#> The HSM returns this response: <29#BC62A2AD72516EA1#A68C#>\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 19 - Translate Working Key for Local Storage\n\n- **Command ID:** `19`\n- **Title:** Translate Working Key for Local Storage\n- **PDF Pages:** 178 - 179\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 19 translates a Working Key from Base Key encryption (without a variant) to MFK encryption for local storage and subsequent use. This command imports a Working Key from a network that does not use Atalla variants.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Disabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<19#Variant#Base Key#Working Key#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<29#Working Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 19 |\n| 1 | Variant | 1, 2 | The MFK variant which encrypts the Base Key.This field contains a decimal number in the range of 0 - 31. See “Variant” on page 59 for a list of supported variants. |\n| 2 | Base Key | 16, 32 | The Base Key encrypted under variant of the MFK specified in field 1. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n| 3 | Working Key | 16, 32 | The Working Key encrypted under the Base Key. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 29 |\n| 1 | Working Key | 16, 32 | The Working Key encrypted under the variant of the MFK specified in field 1 of the command. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters. |\n| 2 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The Working Key check digits are the leftmost four hexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros under the Working Key. If option 88 is enabled, the leftmost six check digits are returned. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- Option 65 must be enabled if command field 1 contains the number 0.\n- Encrypt the Base Key under the appropriate variant of the MFK. Variant Example The 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A. See “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n- Variant: 1\n- Clear-text Base Key: 0123 4567 89AB CDEF The Base Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK: AE86 D417 E64E 07E0\n- Clear-text PIN Encryption Key: FEDC BA98 7654 3210 The PIN encryption key encrypted under the Base Key: 12C6 26AF 058B 433B The command looks like this: <19#1#AE86D417E64E07E0#12C626AF058B433B#> The HSM returns this response: <29#BC62A2AD72516EA1#A68C#>\n\n"
    },
