    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 1D - Translate Communications Key for Local Storage, Specific Variant\n\n- **Command ID:** `1D`\n- **Title:** Translate Communications Key for Local Storage, Specific Variant\n- **PDF Pages:** 185 - 186\n\n---\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Disabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1D#Key Usage#Base Key#Working Key#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2D#Working Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 1D |\n| 1 | Key Usage | 1 | The variant of the MFK under which the Working Key will be encrypted. This field contains a number in the range of 1 - 3, where: 1 = PIN Encryption Key (KPE) 2 = Data Encryption Key (KD) 3 = Message Authentication Key (KMAC) |\n| 2 | Base Key | 16 | The Base Key encrypted under variant 2 of the MFK. This key encrypts the Working Key. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n| 3 | Working Key | 16 | The Working Key encrypted under the Base Key. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 2D |\n| 1 | Working Key | 16 | The Working Key encrypted under the variant of the MFK specified in field 1 of the command. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters. |\n| 2 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The Working Key check digits are the leftmost four hexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros under the Working Key. If option 88 is enabled, the leftmost six check digits are returned. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- All keys must be 1key-3DES keys. Variant Example The 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A. See “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values. Translate a PIN Encryption Key\n- Variant: 1\n- Clear-text Base Key: 1010 2020 4040 8080 The Base Key encrypted under variant 2 of the MFK: 1693 C76D 5493 D733\n- Clear-text PIN Encryption Key: E0E0 D0D0 B0B0 7070 The PIN Encryption Key encrypted under the Base Key: 3758 EB8D B208 C875 The command looks like this: <1D#1#1693C76D5493D733#3758EB8DB208C875#> The HSM returns this response: <2D#F0224DB34CB2E9B9#19D7#>\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 1D - Translate Communications Key for Local Storage, Specific Variant\n\n- **Command ID:** `1D`\n- **Title:** Translate Communications Key for Local Storage, Specific Variant\n- **PDF Pages:** 185 - 186\n\n---\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Disabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<1D#Key Usage#Base Key#Working Key#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<2D#Working Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 1D |\n| 1 | Key Usage | 1 | The variant of the MFK under which the Working Key will be encrypted. This field contains a number in the range of 1 - 3, where: 1 = PIN Encryption Key (KPE) 2 = Data Encryption Key (KD) 3 = Message Authentication Key (KMAC) |\n| 2 | Base Key | 16 | The Base Key encrypted under variant 2 of the MFK. This key encrypts the Working Key. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n| 3 | Working Key | 16 | The Working Key encrypted under the Base Key. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 2D |\n| 1 | Working Key | 16 | The Working Key encrypted under the variant of the MFK specified in field 1 of the command. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters. |\n| 2 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The Working Key check digits are the leftmost four hexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros under the Working Key. If option 88 is enabled, the leftmost six check digits are returned. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- All keys must be 1key-3DES keys. Variant Example The 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A. See “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values. Translate a PIN Encryption Key\n- Variant: 1\n- Clear-text Base Key: 1010 2020 4040 8080 The Base Key encrypted under variant 2 of the MFK: 1693 C76D 5493 D733\n- Clear-text PIN Encryption Key: E0E0 D0D0 B0B0 7070 The PIN Encryption Key encrypted under the Base Key: 3758 EB8D B208 C875 The command looks like this: <1D#1#1693C76D5493D733#3758EB8DB208C875#> The HSM returns this response: <2D#F0224DB34CB2E9B9#19D7#>\n\n"
    },
