        "id": "key-block-protection-74-90-key-106-110",
        "name": {
          "es": "Key Block Protection 74, 90, Key 106, 110",
          "en": "Key Block Protection 74, 90, Key 106, 110"
        },
        "description": {
          "es": "The value of the KBPK encrypted under the MFK. This key derives the encryption and MAC keys that protect the working key. The strength of the KBPK must be equal to or greater than the strength of the working key to import. This key must be a 128, 192, or 256 bit AES key. Headers Supported:  Only KBPKs with the following headers are supported in this command: 3kJD*000, where * = E, N, or S.  Headers supported when option E2 is enabled are 3kJD*E000, 3kJN*000, where * = E, N, or S. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII",
          "en": "The value of the KBPK encrypted under the MFK. This key derives the encryption and MAC keys that protect the working key. The strength of the KBPK must be equal to or greater than the strength of the working key to import. This key must be a 128, 192, or 256 bit AES key. Headers Supported:  Only KBPKs with the following headers are supported in this command: 3kJD*000, where * = E, N, or S.  Headers supported when option E2 is enabled are 3kJD*E000, 3kJN*000, where * = E, N, or S. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII"
        },
