    "source": "Utimaco Atalla AT1000 Command Reference Manual v8.60 (Command 313)",
    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 313 - Verify PAN Binding Token\n\n- **Command ID:** `313`\n- **Title:** Verify PAN Binding Token\n- **PDF Pages:** 1115 - 1116\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 313 verifies the PAN Binding token created in command 312.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Disabled | AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<313#Algorithm#PAN Binding Key#[Tokenized PAN]#[PAN]#PAN Binding Token#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<413#PAN Binding Token#Check Digits#>\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command ID | 3 | 313 |\n| 1 | Algorithm | 1 | This field indicates the MAC algorithm to use: 2 = AES CMAC Legal Characters: 2 |\n| 2 | PAN Binding Key | 74, 90, 106, 110 | The CMAC Key encrypted under the MFK. Headers Supported: 3BJN*00B, 3BJV*00B, where * = E, N, or S. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n| 3 | [Tokenized PAN] | 0,12-19 | The tokenized PAN value. If only \"compact\" PIN blocks are supported (e.g. ISO-0 and ISO-3), then this can be either the 12 digit ANSI PAN or the full tokenized card number. If ISO-4 may be supported, include the full card number. Legal Characters: 0-9 |\n| 4 | [PAN] | 0,12-19 | The value of the actual PAN. If only \"compact\" PIN blocks are supported (e.g. ISO-0 and ISO-3), then this can be either the 12 digit ANSI PAN or the full tokenized card number. If ISO-4 may be supported, include the full card number. Legal Characters: 0-9 |\n| 5 | PAN Binding Token | 46-60 | The generated PAN Binding Token. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 3 | 413 |\n| 1 | Verification Indicator | 1 | Indicates the result of checking the binding: Y: everything verified correctly. N: The MAC did not verify. 3: The PAN provided in field 4 is not present in the PAN binding token. 4: the PAN provided in field 5 is not present in the PAN binding token. Legal Characters: Y, N, 3, 4 |\n| 2 | Check Digits | 10 | The check digits are the leftmost ten digits from CMAC of a zero block. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- When command field 6 contains the ANSI PAN, the result will be correct if the original binding was created using either the ANSI PAN or the full card number. If this PAN contains the full card number, then the result will verify only if the original binding used the full PAN. AKB AES MFK Example The AES Master File Key is: 2ABC3DEF45670189 98107645FED3CBA2 0123456789ABCDEF FEDCBA9876543210 check digits = B9BCAB7B62. See “AES Key (256-bit)” on page 1374 for component values.\n- The clear text CMAC Key = 00001111222233334444555566667777, check digits = FEF900C20E The CMAC Key in AKB format 3BJNE00B,2555E8880E29821FC38300C621DBBD39,DA8E3CD9A847FFC0CFD438A1E087BF62\n- Tokenized PAN = 1234567890123456789\n- PAN = 9876543210987654\n- PAN Binding Token = 01191234567890123456789169876543210987654FB6719C26E4FF844B The command looks like this: <313#2#3BJNE00B,2555E8880E29821FC38300C621DBBD39,DA8E3CD9A847FFC0CFD438A1E087B F62#1234567890123456789#9876543210987654#0119123456789012345678916987654321098 7654FB6719C26E4FF844B#> The HSM returns this response: <413#Y#FEF900C20E#>\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 313 - Verify PAN Binding Token\n\n- **Command ID:** `313`\n- **Title:** Verify PAN Binding Token\n- **PDF Pages:** 1115 - 1116\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 313 verifies the PAN Binding token created in command 312.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Disabled | AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<313#Algorithm#PAN Binding Key#[Tokenized PAN]#[PAN]#PAN Binding Token#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<413#PAN Binding Token#Check Digits#>\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command ID | 3 | 313 |\n| 1 | Algorithm | 1 | This field indicates the MAC algorithm to use: 2 = AES CMAC Legal Characters: 2 |\n| 2 | PAN Binding Key | 74, 90, 106, 110 | The CMAC Key encrypted under the MFK. Headers Supported: 3BJN*00B, 3BJV*00B, where * = E, N, or S. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n| 3 | [Tokenized PAN] | 0,12-19 | The tokenized PAN value. If only \"compact\" PIN blocks are supported (e.g. ISO-0 and ISO-3), then this can be either the 12 digit ANSI PAN or the full tokenized card number. If ISO-4 may be supported, include the full card number. Legal Characters: 0-9 |\n| 4 | [PAN] | 0,12-19 | The value of the actual PAN. If only \"compact\" PIN blocks are supported (e.g. ISO-0 and ISO-3), then this can be either the 12 digit ANSI PAN or the full tokenized card number. If ISO-4 may be supported, include the full card number. Legal Characters: 0-9 |\n| 5 | PAN Binding Token | 46-60 | The generated PAN Binding Token. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 3 | 413 |\n| 1 | Verification Indicator | 1 | Indicates the result of checking the binding: Y: everything verified correctly. N: The MAC did not verify. 3: The PAN provided in field 4 is not present in the PAN binding token. 4: the PAN provided in field 5 is not present in the PAN binding token. Legal Characters: Y, N, 3, 4 |\n| 2 | Check Digits | 10 | The check digits are the leftmost ten digits from CMAC of a zero block. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- When command field 6 contains the ANSI PAN, the result will be correct if the original binding was created using either the ANSI PAN or the full card number. If this PAN contains the full card number, then the result will verify only if the original binding used the full PAN. AKB AES MFK Example The AES Master File Key is: 2ABC3DEF45670189 98107645FED3CBA2 0123456789ABCDEF FEDCBA9876543210 check digits = B9BCAB7B62. See “AES Key (256-bit)” on page 1374 for component values.\n- The clear text CMAC Key = 00001111222233334444555566667777, check digits = FEF900C20E The CMAC Key in AKB format 3BJNE00B,2555E8880E29821FC38300C621DBBD39,DA8E3CD9A847FFC0CFD438A1E087BF62\n- Tokenized PAN = 1234567890123456789\n- PAN = 9876543210987654\n- PAN Binding Token = 01191234567890123456789169876543210987654FB6719C26E4FF844B The command looks like this: <313#2#3BJNE00B,2555E8880E29821FC38300C621DBBD39,DA8E3CD9A847FFC0CFD438A1E087B F62#1234567890123456789#9876543210987654#0119123456789012345678916987654321098 7654FB6719C26E4FF844B#> The HSM returns this response: <413#Y#FEF900C20E#>\n\n"
    },
    "pairedCode": "413"
