      "en": "# Command 33 - Translate PIN, ANSI to ANSI\n\n- **Command ID:** `33`\n- **Title:** Translate PIN, ANSI to ANSI\n- **PDF Pages:** 280 - 283\n\n---\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 33 |\n| 1 | 13 | 1 | The format of the incoming PIN block is ANSI. The format of the outgoing PIN block is PIN/PAD. |\n| 2 | 🌸 Incoming PIN Encryption Key (AKB) | 74 | The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under the MFK. This key encrypted the incoming PIN block. This field contains 74 printable ASCII characters, or a volatile table location. Headers Supported: 3DES MFK 1PUN*000, 1PUD*000, where * = E or N. Headers Supported: AES MFK 3PUN*000, 3PUD*000, where * = E, N, or S. |\n| 2 | 🟪 Incoming PIN Encryption Key (Variant) | 16, 32 | The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK. This key encrypted the incoming PIN block. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n| 3 | Outgoing PIN Encryption Key | 74 | The outgoing PIN Encryption Key encrypted under the MFK. This key encrypts the outgoing PIN/PAD PIN block. This field contains 74 printable ASCII characters, or a volatile table location. Headers Supported: 3DES MFK 1PUN*000, 1PUE*000, where * = E or N. Headers Supported: AES MFK 3PUN*000, 3PUE*000, where * = E, N, or S. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 43 |\n| 1 | Outgoing PIN Block | 16 | The ANSI PIN Block encrypted under the Outgoing PIN Encryption Key. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters. When a PIN sanity error is detected, the value in this field may not be correct. When a PIN sanity error is detected, and option 4B is enabled, this field will contain 16 zeros. |\n| 2 | Sanity Check Indicator | 1 | The sanity check indicator. Option 4B specifies the type of PIN sanity test to be performed on the incoming PIN block. This field can contain one uppercase character, where: Y = PIN block passes the sanity check N = PIN failed the sanity test. Or the length of the PIN is out of range and PIN-length error reporting has not been enabled. See “PIN sanity error” on page 73 and option “A1” on page 1415 L = The length of the PIN is out of range. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n\n#### 🌸 AKB Usage Notes\n\n- When option 49 is enabled, an error response is returned if the length of the Outgoing PIN Encryption Key is not equal-to or greater-than the length of the Incoming PIN Encryption Key. When either option 46 or 47 is enabled, both fields 5 and 6 must contain the same 12 PAN digits. This command supports 1key-3DES (single-length) keys only if 6C is enabled. The Incoming and Outgoing PIN Encryption Keys can be a 3key-3DES key only when the HSM is configured with a 3key-3DES key MFK. AKB 3DES MFK Example The 3key-3DES Master File Key is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2 0123 4567 89AB CDEF, check digits = B196. See “3key-3DES Key (Triple-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n- Clear-text incoming PIN Encryption Key: 07CE A74F 4607 5D8F The incoming PIN Encryption Key in AKB format: 1PUNE000,24E42C54BA2DD3F1781BBBB84298B1193BD0CDFCF431B0C0,C475179371FDBE43\n- Clear-text outgoing PIN Encryption Key: D029 23D9 AD4F E90B The outgoing PIN Encryption Key in AKB format: 1PUNE000,9BA4CBE61A4247783D4DED9A7E2FAD879CAC53AF657A4508,7ED69570CDE54F30\n- Clear-text PIN block: 0453 55F8 BEF7 EBBA The PIN block encrypted under the incoming PIN Encryption Key: 5196 681F 910C 408C.\n- Incoming PAN digits: 1207 4108 1445\n- Outgoing PAN digits: 2074 1081 4457 The command looks like this: <33#11#1PUNE000,24E42C54BA2DD3F1781BBBB84298B1193BD0CDFCF431B0C0,C475179371FDB E43#1PUNE000,9BA4CBE61A4247783D4DED9A7E2FAD879CAC53AF657A4508,7ED69570CDE54F30 #5196681F910C408C#120741081445#207410814457#> The HSM returns this response: <43#7BB41A6FAA3BF848#Y#> AKB AES MFK Example The AES Master File Key is: 2ABC3DEF45670189 98107645FED3CBA2 0123456789ABCDEF FEDCBA9876543210, check digits = B9BCAB7B62. See “AES Key (256-bit)” on page 1374 for component values.\n\n#### 🟪 Variant Usage Notes\n\n- When option 49 is enabled, an error response is returned if the length of the Outgoing PIN Encryption Key is not equal-to or greater-than the length of the Incoming PIN Encryption Key. When either option 46 or 47 is enabled, both fields 5 and 6 must contain the same 12 PAN digits.\n- Clear-text incoming PIN Encryption Key: 07CE A74F 4607 5D8F The incoming PIN Encryption Key in AKB format: 3PUNE000,B89EBDA08D31D905E0883883443F4F6F9A4A82139C833FA7,D2D1CE0B3DADB0BB\n- Clear-text outgoing PIN Encryption Key: D029 23D9 AD4F E90B The outgoing PIN Encryption Key in AKB format: 3PUNE000,E9F5240B74CCD2AEB44EA23BF13D89D0EC93F7028EA03747,5C63B64FCAB4BA54\n- Clear-text PIN block: 0453 55F8 BEF7 EBBA The PIN block encrypted under the incoming PIN Encryption Key: 5196 681F 910C 408C.\n- Incoming PAN digits: 1207 4108 1445\n- Outgoing PAN digits: 2074 1081 4457 The command looks like this: <33#11#3PUNE000,B89EBDA08D31D905E0883883443F4F6F9A4A82139C833FA7,D2D1CE0B3DADB 0BB#3PUNE000,E9F5240B74CCD2AEB44EA23BF13D89D0EC93F7028EA03747,5C63B64FCAB4BA54 #5196681F910C408C#120741081445#207410814457#> The HSM returns this response: <43#7BB41A6FAA3BF848#Y#> Variant Example The 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A. See “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n- Clear-text incoming PIN Encryption Key: 07CE A74F 4607 5D8F 0000 1111 2222 3333 The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK: 3B42 CA42 78E2 DDE1 47F1 02C2 D4DE 29C4\n- Clear-text outgoing PIN Encryption Key: D029 23D9 AD4F E90B 5555 6666 7777 8888 The outgoing PIN Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK: 83CB EFA7 10C6 639F 1DE1 CF68 9E96 99D6\n- Clear-text PIN block: 0453 55F8 BEF7 EBBA The PIN block encrypted under the incoming PIN Encryption Key: F4DB 98CB C7D2 DC14\n- Incoming PAN digits: 1207 4108 1445\n- Outgoing PAN digits: 2074 1081 4457 The command looks like this: <33#11#3B42CA4278E2DDE147F102C2D4DE29C4#83CBEFA710C6639F1DE1CF689E9699D6#F4DB9 8CBC7D2DC14#120741081445#207410814457#> The HSM returns this response: <43#CBC0F5BC0ED28BBD#Y#> 33 - Translate PIN, ANSI to PIN/Pad Command 33 translates an encrypted ANSI PIN block from encryption under an Incoming PIN Encryption Key to encryption under an Outgoing PIN Encryption Key. The Outgoing PIN block is a PIN/PAD PIN block. Key Type Default Setting MFK Type AKB Disabled 3DES, AES Variant Disablec 3DES Command <33#13#Incoming PIN Encryption Key#Outgoing PIN Encryption Key#PIN Block# PAD#ANSI PAN Digits#> Response <43#Outgoing PIN Block#Sanity Check Indicator#>[CRLF] Command description Colors specific to key management method No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant Field Contents Length Description 0 Command identifier 2 33 1 13 1 The format of the incoming PIN block is ANSI. The format of the outgoing PIN block is PIN/PAD. 2 Incoming PIN Encryption 74 The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under the MFK. Key This key encrypted the incoming PIN block. This field contains 74 printable ASCII characters, or a volatile table location. Headers Supported: 3DES MFK 1PUN*000, 1PUD*000, where * = E or N. Headers Supported: AES MFK 3PUN*000, 3PUD*000, where * = E, N, or S. 16, 32 The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK. This key encrypted the incoming PIN block. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. 3 Outgoing PIN Encryption 74 The outgoing PIN Encryption Key encrypted under the MFK. Key This key encrypts the outgoing PIN/PAD PIN block. This field contains 74 printable ASCII characters, or a volatile table location. Headers Supported: 3DES MFK 1PUN*000, 1PUE*000, where * = E or N. Headers Supported: AES MFK 3PUN*000, 3PUE*000, where * = E, N, or S.\n\n"
