      "en": "# Command 33 - Translate PIN, ANSI to PIN/Pad\n\n- **Command ID:** `33`\n- **Title:** Translate PIN, ANSI to PIN/Pad\n- **PDF Pages:** 284 - 287\n\n---\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 33 |\n| 1 | 19 | 1 | The format of the incoming PIN block is ANSI. The format of the outgoing PIN block is IBM 4731. |\n| 2 | 🌸 Incoming PIN Encryption Key (AKB) | 74 | The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under the MFK. This key encrypted the incoming PIN block. This field contains 74 printable ASCII characters, or a volatile table location. Headers Supported: 3DES MFK 1PUN*000, 1PUD*000, where * = E or N. Headers Supported: AES MFK 3PUN*000, 3PUD*000, where * = E, N, or S. |\n| 2 | 🟪 Incoming PIN Encryption Key (Variant) | 16, 32 | The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK. This key encrypted the incoming PIN block. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n| 3 | Outgoing PIN Encryption Key | 74 | The outgoing PIN Encryption Key encrypted under the MFK. This key encrypts the outgoing PIN/PAD PIN block. This field contains 74 printable ASCII characters, or a volatile table location. Headers Supported: 3DES MFK 1PUN*000, 1PUE*000, where * = E or N. Headers Supported: AES MFK 3PUN*000, 3PUE*000, where * = E, N, or S. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 43 |\n| 1 | Outgoing PIN Block | 16 | The PIN/PAD PIN Block encrypted under the Outgoing PIN Encryption Key. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters. When a PIN sanity error is detected, the value in this field may not be correct. |\n| 2 | Sanity Check Indicator | 1 | The sanity check indicator. Option 4B specifies the type of PIN sanity test to be performed on the incoming PIN block. This field can contain one uppercase character, where: Y = PIN block passes the sanity check N = PIN failed the sanity test. Or the length of the PIN is out of range and PIN-length error reporting has not been enabled. See “PIN sanity error” on page 73 and option “A1” on page 1415 L = The length of the PIN is out of range. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n\n#### 🌸 AKB Usage Notes\n\n- When option 49 is enabled, an error response is returned if the length of the Outgoing PIN Encryption Key is not equal-to or greater-than the length of the Incoming PIN Encryption Key. When either option 46 or 47 is enabled, the HSM will return an error response. This command supports 1key-3DES (single-length) keys only if 6C is enabled.\n\n#### 🟪 Variant Usage Notes\n\n- When option 49 is enabled, an error response is returned if the length of the Outgoing PIN Encryption Key is not equal-to or greater-than the length of the Incoming PIN Encryption Key. When either option 46 or 47 is enabled, the HSM will return an error response. The Incoming and Outgoing PIN Encryption Keys can be a 3key-3DES key only when the HSM is configured with a 3key-3DES key MFK. AKB 3DES MFK Example The 3key-3DES Master File Key is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2 0123 4567 89AB CDEF, check digits = B196. See “3key-3DES Key (Triple-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n- Clear-text incoming PIN Encryption Key: 07CE A74F 4607 5D8F The incoming PIN Encryption Key in AKB format: 1PUNE000,24E42C54BA2DD3F1781BBBB84298B1193BD0CDFCF431B0C0,C475179371FDBE43\n- Clear-text outgoing PIN Encryption Key: D029 23D9 AD4F E90B The outgoing PIN Encryption Key in AKB format: 1PUNE000,9BA4CBE61A4247783D4DED9A7E2FAD879CAC53AF657A4508,7ED69570CDE54F30\n- Clear-text incoming PIN block: 045355F8BEF7EBBA The incoming PIN block encrypted under the incoming PIN Encryption Key: 5196 681F 910C 408C\n- Outgoing Pad character: D\n- Incoming PAN: 1207 4108 1445 The command looks like this: <33#13#1PUNE000,24E42C54BA2DD3F1781BBBB84298B1193BD0CDFCF431B0C0,C475179371FDB E43#1PUNE000,9BA4CBE61A4247783D4DED9A7E2FAD879CAC53AF657A4508,7ED69570CDE54F30 #5196681F910C408C#D#120741081445#> The HSM returns this response: <43#F9081E2639080784#Y#> AKB AES MFK Example The AES Master File Key is: 2ABC3DEF45670189 98107645FED3CBA2 0123456789ABCDEF FEDCBA9876543210, check digits = B9BCAB7B62. See “AES Key (256-bit)” on page 1374 for component values.\n- Clear-text incoming PIN Encryption Key: 07CE A74F 4607 5D8F The incoming PIN Encryption Key in AKB format: 3PUNE000,B89EBDA08D31D905E0883883443F4F6F9A4A82139C833FA7,D2D1CE0B3DADB0BB\n- Clear-text outgoing PIN Encryption Key: D029 23D9 AD4F E90B The outgoing PIN Encryption Key in AKB format: 3PUNE000,E9F5240B74CCD2AEB44EA23BF13D89D0EC93F7028EA03747,5C63B64FCAB4BA54\n- Clear-text incoming PIN block: 045355F8BEF7EBBA The incoming PIN block encrypted under the incoming PIN Encryption Key: 5196 681F 910C 408C\n- Outgoing Pad character: D\n- Incoming PAN: 1207 4108 1445 The command looks like this: <33#13#3PUNE000,B89EBDA08D31D905E0883883443F4F6F9A4A82139C833FA7,D2D1CE0B3DADB 0BB#3PUNE000,E9F5240B74CCD2AEB44EA23BF13D89D0EC93F7028EA03747,5C63B64FCAB4BA54 #5196681F910C408C#D#120741081445#> The HSM returns this response: <43#F9081E2639080784#Y#> Variant Example The 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A. See “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n- Clear-text incoming PIN Encryption Key: 0123456789ABCDEF 0000111122223333 The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK: AE86D417E64E07E047F102C2D4DE29C4\n- Clear-text outgoing PIN Encryption Key: 4567 ABCD EF12 3890 5555 6666 7777 8888 The outgoing PIN Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK: 5E970C0BFB49402C1DE1CF689E9699D6\n- Clear-text incoming PIN block: 045355F8BEF7EBBA The incoming PIN block encrypted under the incoming PIN Encryption Key: 2299CD5D3804E247\n- Outgoing Pad character: D\n- Incoming PAN: 120741081445 The command looks like this: <33#13#AE86D417E64E07E047F102C2D4DE29C4#5E970C0BFB49402C1DE1CF689E9699D6#2299C D5D3804E247#D#120741081445#> The HSM returns this response: <43#D3F5F0561FCAAE78#Y#> 33 - Translate PIN, ANSI to IBM 4731 Command 33 translates an encrypted ANSI PIN block from encryption under an Incoming PIN Encryption Key to encryption under an Outgoing PIN Encryption Key. The Outgoing PIN block is an IBM 4731 PIN block. Key Type Default Setting MFK Type AKB Disabled 3DES, AES Variant Disabled 3DES Command <33#19#Incoming PIN Encryption Key#Outgoing PIN Encryption Key#PIN Block# ANSI PAN Digits#Pad#Outgoing ICV#Communications Key#> Response <43#Outgoing PIN Block#Sanity Check Indicator#>[CRLF] Command description Colors specific to key management method No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant Field Contents Length Description 0 Command identifier 2 33 1 19 1 The format of the incoming PIN block is ANSI. The format of the outgoing PIN block is IBM 4731. 2 Incoming PIN Encryption 74 The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under the MFK. Key This key encrypted the incoming PIN block. This field contains 74 printable ASCII characters, or a volatile table location. Headers Supported: 3DES MFK 1PUN*000, 1PUD*000, where * = E or N. Headers Supported: AES MFK 3PUN*000, 3PUD*000, where * = E, N, or S. 16, 32 The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK. This key encrypted the incoming PIN block. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. 3 Outgoing PIN Encryption 74 The outgoing PIN Encryption Key encrypted under the MFK. Key This key encrypts the outgoing PIN/PAD PIN block. This field contains 74 printable ASCII characters, or a volatile table location. Headers Supported: 3DES MFK 1PUN*000, 1PUE*000, where * = E or N. Headers Supported: AES MFK 3PUN*000, 3PUE*000, where * = E, N, or S.\n\n"
