      "en": "# Command 33 - Translate PIN, IBM 3624 to IBM 3624\n\n- **Command ID:** `33`\n- **Title:** Translate PIN, IBM 3624 to IBM 3624\n- **PDF Pages:** 293 - 298\n\n---\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 43 |\n| 1 | Outgoing PIN Block | 16 | The IBM 3624 PIN Block encrypted under the Outgoing PIN Encryption Key. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters. When a PIN sanity error is detected, the value in this field may not be correct. |\n| 2 | Sanity Check Indicator | 1 | The sanity check indicator. Option 4B specifies the type of PIN sanity test to be performed on the incoming PIN block. This field can contain one uppercase character, where: Y = PIN block passes the sanity check N = PIN failed the sanity test. Or the length of the PIN is out of range and PIN-length error reporting has not been enabled. See “PIN sanity error” on page 73 and option “A1” on page 1415 L = The length of the PIN is out of range. |\n| 3 | [IBM 3624 Sequence Number#] | [2] | This field is optional. It is only present when the PIN Block Format is 2. When present, It contains the 2 hexadecimal characters of the IBM 3624 Sequence Number. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n\n#### 🌸 AKB Usage Notes\n\n- When option 49 is enabled, an error response is returned if the length of the Outgoing PIN Encryption Key is not equal-to or greater-than the length of the Incoming PIN Encryption Key.\n\n#### 🟪 Variant Usage Notes\n\n- When option 49 is enabled, an error response is returned if the length of the Outgoing PIN Encryption Key is not equal-to or greater-than the length of the Incoming PIN Encryption Key. When either option 46 or 47 is enabled, the HSM will When either option 46 or 47 is enabled, the HSM return an error response. will return an error response. This command supports 1key-3DES (single-length) keys only if 6C is enabled. The Incoming and Outgoing PIN Encryption Keys can be a 3key-3DES key only when the HSM is configured with a 3key-3DES key MFK. AKB 3DES MFK Example The 3key-3DES Master File Key is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2 0123 4567 89AB CDEF, check digits = B196. See “3key-3DES Key (Triple-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n- Clear-text incoming PIN Encryption Key: 07CE A74F 4607 5D8F The incoming PIN Encryption Key in AKB format: 1PUNE000,24E42C54BA2DD3F1781BBBB84298B1193BD0CDFCF431B0C0,C475179371FDBE43\n- Clear-text outgoing PIN Encryption Key: D029 23D9 AD4F E90B The outgoing PIN Encryption Key in AKB format: 1PUNE000,9BA4CBE61A4247783D4DED9A7E2FAD879CAC53AF657A4508,7ED69570CDE54F30\n- Encrypted incoming PIN block: 9864 AB86 5904 8084 B8\n- Incoming pad character: B.\n- Clear-text incoming Communications Key: A15D BAFD F119 F701. The incoming Communications Key in AKB format: 1DDNE000,740B352ADA6934929EECA387D23104F5582D59EF93C3AB88,571989DBB9DBC083\n- Outgoing pad character: D\n- Clear-text outgoing Communications Key: F72B 85D0 302D 448A The outgoing Communications Key in AKB format: 1DDNE000,21FC89139C29187EA8289644DB94778329EB33A75B5E7957,7BA5D13D8292D947 The command looks like this: <33#22#1PUNE000,24E42C54BA2DD3F1781BBBB84298B1193BD0CDFCF431B0C0,C475179371FDB E43#1PUNE000,9BA4CBE61A4247783D4DED9A7E2FAD879CAC53AF657A4508,7ED69570CDE54F30 #9864AB8659048084B8#B#1DDNE000,740B352ADA6934929EECA387D23104F5582D59EF93C3AB8 8,571989DBB9DBC083#D#1DDNE000,21FC89139C29187EA8289644DB94778329EB33A75B5E7957,7BA5D13D8292D947#> The HSM returns this response: <43#843322E77167AE5384#Y#99#> AKB AES MFK Example The AES Master File Key is: 2ABC3DEF45670189 98107645FED3CBA2 0123456789ABCDEF FEDCBA9876543210, check digits = B9BCAB7B62. See “AES Key (256-bit)” on page 1374 for component values.\n- Clear-text incoming PIN Encryption Key: 07CE A74F 4607 5D8F The incoming PIN Encryption Key in AKB format: 3PUNE000,B89EBDA08D31D905E0883883443F4F6F9A4A82139C833FA7,D2D1CE0B3DADB0BB\n- Clear-text outgoing PIN Encryption Key: D029 23D9 AD4F E90B The outgoing PIN Encryption Key in AKB format: 3PUNE000,E9F5240B74CCD2AEB44EA23BF13D89D0EC93F7028EA03747,5C63B64FCAB4BA54\n- Encrypted incoming PIN block: 9864 AB86 5904 8084 B8\n- Incoming pad character: B.\n- Clear-text incoming Communications Key: A15D BAFD F119 F701. The incoming Communications Key in AKB format: 3DDNE000,C0A2DB4BF86554AD6D7DC3BFA22B7734BB16823614E92007,C8E2816190D305D4\n- Outgoing pad character: D\n- Clear-text outgoing Communications Key: F72B 85D0 302D 448A The outgoing Communications Key in AKB format: 3DDNE000,8AA3F3133C4C5F30DDDD67DD60C5AD9CE5E56B8BA6C4485F,59D9C65FA98430F4 The command looks like this: <33#22#3PUNE000,B89EBDA08D31D905E0883883443F4F6F9A4A82139C833FA7,D2D1CE0B3DADB 0BB#3PUNE000,E9F5240B74CCD2AEB44EA23BF13D89D0EC93F7028EA03747,5C63B64FCAB4BA54 #9864AB8659048084B8#B#3DDNE000,C0A2DB4BF86554AD6D7DC3BFA22B7734BB16823614E9200 7,C8E2816190D305D4#D#3DDNE000,8AA3F3133C4C5F30DDDD67DD60C5AD9CE5E56B8BA6C4485F,59D9C65FA98430F4#> The HSM returns this response: <43#843322E77167AE5384#Y#99#> Variant Example The 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A. See “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n- Clear-text incoming PIN Encryption Key: 07CE A74F 4607 5D8F The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK: 3B42 CA42 78E2 DDE1\n- Clear-text outgoing PIN Encryption Key: D029 23D9 AD4F E90B The outgoing PIN Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK: 83CB EFA7 10C6 639F\n- Encrypted incoming PIN block: 9864 AB86 5904 8084 B8\n- Incoming pad character: B\n- Clear-text incoming Communications Key: A15D BAFD F119 F701 The incoming Communications Key encrypted under variant 2 of the MFK: 306D0D8C8A2E6414\n- Outgoing pad character: D\n- Clear-text outgoing Communications Key: F72B 85D0 302D 448A The outgoing Communications Key encrypted under variant 2 of the MFK: 1646 F963 48BD 4800 The command looks like this: <33#22#3B42CA4278E2DDE1#83CBEFA710C6639F#9864AB8659048084B8#B#306D0D8C8A2E6414 #D#1646F96348BD4800#> The HSM returns this response: <43#843322E77167AE5384#Y#99#> 33 - Translate PIN, IBM 3624 to PIN/Pad Command 33 translates an encrypted IBM 3624 PIN block from encryption under an Incoming PIN Encryption Key to encryption under an Outgoing PIN Encryption Key. The outgoing PIN block is a PIN/Pad PIN block. Key Type Default Setting MFK Type AKB Disabled 3DES, AES Variant Disabled 3DES Command <33#23#Incoming PIN Encryption Key#Outgoing PIN Encryption Key#PIN Block# Incoming Pad#Communications Key#Outgoing Pad#> Response <43#Outgoing PIN Block#Sanity Check Indicator#IBM 3624 Sequence Number#>[CRLF] Command description Colors specific to key management method No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant Field Contents Length Description 0 Command identifier 2 33 1 23 1 The format of the incoming PIN block is IBM 3624. The format of the outgoing PIN block is PIN Pad. 2 Incoming PIN Encryption 74 The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under the MFK. Key This key encrypted the incoming PIN block. This field contains 74 printable ASCII characters, or a volatile table location. Headers Supported: 3DES MFK 1PUN*000, 1PUD*000, where * = E or N. Headers Supported: AES MFK 3PUN*000, 3PUD*000, where * = E, N, or S. 16, 32 The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK. This key encrypted the incoming PIN block. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location.\n\n"
