    "source": "Utimaco Atalla AT1000 Command Reference Manual v8.60 (Command 33)",
    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 33 - Translate PIN, PIN/Pad to ANSI\n\n- **Command ID:** `33`\n- **Title:** Translate PIN, PIN/Pad to ANSI\n- **PDF Pages:** 304 - 305\n\n---\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 33 |\n| 1 | 33 | 1 | The format of the incoming PIN block is PIN Pad. The format of the outgoing PIN block is PIN Pad. |\n| 2 | 🌸 Incoming PIN Encryption Key (AKB) | 74 | The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under the MFK. This key encrypted the incoming PIN block. This field contains 74 printable ASCII characters, or a volatile table location. Headers Supported: 3DES MFK 1PUN*000, 1PUD*000, where * = E or N. Headers Supported: AES MFK 3PUN*000, 3PUD*000, where * = E, N, or S. |\n| 2 | 🟪 Incoming PIN Encryption Key (Variant) | 16, 32 | The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK. This key encrypted the incoming PIN block. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- When option 49 is enabled, an error response is returned if the length of the Outgoing PIN Encryption Key is not equal-to or greater-than the length of the Incoming PIN Encryption Key.\n- When either option 46 or 47 is enabled, the HSM will return an error response.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nClear-text incoming PIN Encryption Key: 4455445544554455\n\nClear-text outgoing PIN Encryption Key: 2233223322332233\n\nEncrypted PIN block: FBBAA4940B07C982\n\nIncoming pad character: X\n\nANSI PAN Digits: 999999000000\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<33#31#72E7AEF691471872#8C2A7691A708A88D#FBBAA4940B07C982#X#999999000000#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<43#2C39AECDB8EA47EC#Y#>\n```\n\n```\n<33#33#Incoming  PIN  Encryption  Key#Outgoing  PIN  Encryption  Key#PIN  Block#Incoming  Pad#Outgoing  Pad#>\n```\n\n```\n<43#Outgoing PIN  Block#Sanity  Check  Indicator#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 33 - Translate PIN, PIN/Pad to ANSI\n\n- **Command ID:** `33`\n- **Title:** Translate PIN, PIN/Pad to ANSI\n- **PDF Pages:** 304 - 305\n\n---\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 33 |\n| 1 | 33 | 1 | The format of the incoming PIN block is PIN Pad. The format of the outgoing PIN block is PIN Pad. |\n| 2 | 🌸 Incoming PIN Encryption Key (AKB) | 74 | The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under the MFK. This key encrypted the incoming PIN block. This field contains 74 printable ASCII characters, or a volatile table location. Headers Supported: 3DES MFK 1PUN*000, 1PUD*000, where * = E or N. Headers Supported: AES MFK 3PUN*000, 3PUD*000, where * = E, N, or S. |\n| 2 | 🟪 Incoming PIN Encryption Key (Variant) | 16, 32 | The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK. This key encrypted the incoming PIN block. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- When option 49 is enabled, an error response is returned if the length of the Outgoing PIN Encryption Key is not equal-to or greater-than the length of the Incoming PIN Encryption Key.\n- When either option 46 or 47 is enabled, the HSM will return an error response.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nClear-text incoming PIN Encryption Key: 4455445544554455\n\nClear-text outgoing PIN Encryption Key: 2233223322332233\n\nEncrypted PIN block: FBBAA4940B07C982\n\nIncoming pad character: X\n\nANSI PAN Digits: 999999000000\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<33#31#72E7AEF691471872#8C2A7691A708A88D#FBBAA4940B07C982#X#999999000000#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<43#2C39AECDB8EA47EC#Y#>\n```\n\n```\n<33#33#Incoming  PIN  Encryption  Key#Outgoing  PIN  Encryption  Key#PIN  Block#Incoming  Pad#Outgoing  Pad#>\n```\n\n```\n<43#Outgoing PIN  Block#Sanity  Check  Indicator#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n"
    },
