          "es": "The dCVC3 or dCVC3-PIN verification flag. This field contains 1 uppercase letter, where: Y = the dCVC3 or dCVC3-PIN verified N = the dCVC3 or dCVC3-PIN did not verify Legal Characters: Y or N When command field 7 is empty, this field will contain the generated dCVC3 or dCVC3-PIN. This command always returns a 5-digit CVC3. If a 3 or 4 digit value is needed, take the rightmost digits of the result. For example. if the command returns 12345, the 3-digit CVC3 is 345. Legal Characters: 0-9",
