          "en": "[AKB] The PIN Encryption Key encrypted under the MFK. This key encrypts the ANSI PIN block. This field contains 74 printable ASCII characters, or a volatile table location. ANSI PIN Block is not encrypted under a DUKPT key: Headers Supported: 3DES MFK 1PUN*000, 1PUD*000, where * = E or N. Headers Supported: AES MFK 3PUN*000, 3PUD*000, where * = E, N, or S. ANSI PIN Block is encrypted under a DUKPT key, this field contains the Base Derivation Key encrypted under the MFK. Headers Supported: 3DES MFK 1dDN*000, where * = E or N. Headers Supported: AES MFK 3dDN*000, where * = E, N, or S. | [VARIANT] The PIN Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK. This key encrypts the PIN block. When the ANSI PIN Block is encrypted under a DUKPT key, this field will contain the Base Derivation Key encrypted under variant 8 of the MFK. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters."
