          "en": "The data to be authenticated. When field 2 = 0, the length of this field must be a multiple of 8. When field 2 = 1, 2, or 3, and this field is not a multiple of 8, the HSM will right pad the data with zeros such that the resulting length is a multiple of 8, and then attempt to verify the MAC. When the data format is binary, this field contains 1 - 4096 binary characters. When the data format is unpacked ASCII-Hexadecimal, this field contains an even number of hexadecimal characters."
