      "es": "# Command 71 - Delete Volatile Table Value\n\n- **Command ID:** `71`\n- **Title:** Delete Volatile Table Value\n- **PDF Pages:** 498 - 499\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 71 deletes a value in a specific location within a section of the volatile table. Reference Information: Section 8, “Storing values in the volatile table.”\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<71#Location#[Table Section#]>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<81#Available Locations#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 71 |\n| 1 | 🌸 Location (AKB) | 1 - 4 | The location to be deleted. When deleting a value from section 0, this field contains a number in the range of 0000 - 0999. When deleting a row of a Diebold Number Table from section 1, this field contains a number in the range of 0000 - 9999. |\n| 1 | 🟪 Location (Variant) | 1 - 4 | The location to be deleted. This field contains a number in the range of 0000 - 0999. |\n| 2 | 🌸 [Table Section#] (AKB) | [1] | This field is optional. When present, it specifies the section of the table. This field contains a decimal digit, where: 0 = DES key or conversion table section 1 = Diebold Number Table section When this field is not present, the volatile table section is section 0. |\n| 2 | 🟪 [Table Section#] (Variant) | [0] | This field must not exist |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 81 |\n| 1 | 🌸 Remaining Locations (AKB) | 4 | The number of locations available after this command is executed. This field contains a number in the range of 0000 through 0998. |\n| 1 | 🟪 Remaining Locations (Variant) | 4 | The number of locations available after this command is executed. This field contains a number in the range of 0000 through 9998. |\n\n### Examples\n\nExamples\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<71#35#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<81#0999#>\n```\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<71#437#1#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<81#2743#>\n```\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<71#35#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<81#9999#>\n```\n\n",
