    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 72 - Verify Volatile Table Value\n\n- **Command ID:** `72`\n- **Title:** Verify Volatile Table Value\n- **PDF Pages:** 500 - 502\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 72 retrieves the check digits for the value stored in a specific location within a section of the volatile table. Reference Information: Section 8, “Storing values in the volatile table.”\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<72#Location#[Table Section#]>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<82#Remaining Locations#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 72 |\n| 1 | 🌸 Location (AKB) | 1 - 4 | The location to be verified. When verifying a value from section 0, this field contains a number in the range of 0000 - 0999. When verifying a row of a Diebold Number Table from section 1, this field contains a number in the range of 0000 - 9999. |\n| 1 | 🟪 Location (Variant) | 1 - 4 | The location to be verified. This field contains a number in the range of 0000 - 0999. |\n| 2 | 🌸 [Table Section#] (AKB) | [1] | This field is optional. When present, it specifies the section of the table. This field contains a decimal digit, where: 0 = DES key or conversion table section 1 = Diebold Number Table section When this field is not present, the volatile table section is section 0. |\n| 2 | 🟪 [Table Section#] (Variant) | [0] | This field must not exist |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 82 |\n| 1 | 🌸 Remaining Locations (AKB) | 4 | The number of locations available. This field contains a number in the range of 0000 - 0998. |\n| 1 | 🟪 Remaining Locations (Variant) | 4 | The number of locations available. This field contains a number in the range of 0000 - 9998. |\n| 2 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The key, conversion table, or Diebold Number Table row check digits are the leftmost four hexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros under the key, conversion table, or Diebold Number Table row. If option 88 is enabled, the leftmost six check digits are returned. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n\n#### 🌸 AKB Usage Notes\n\n- The HSM returns an error message <00#0701...> when the specified location is empty.\n- For AKB and Variant key types, the following personality distinctions apply: AKB Examples Verify a DES key in location 17 The command looks like this: <72#17#> The HSM returns this response: <82#1950#D5D4#> Verify a row of a Diebold Number Table in location 438 The command looks like this: <72#438#1#> The HSM returns this response: <82#9950#D5D4#>\n\n#### 🟪 Variant Usage Notes\n\n- 2key-3DES (double-length) keys are loaded in two consecutive locations within the table. When verifying a 2key-3DES (double-length) key, indicate the first of the two locations. For example, if a 2key-3DES (double-length) key is stored in locations 3 and 4, specify location 3 to verify the entire key. Variant Example The command looks like this: <72#17#> The HSM returns this response: <82#1950#D5D4#>\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 72 - Verify Volatile Table Value\n\n- **Command ID:** `72`\n- **Title:** Verify Volatile Table Value\n- **PDF Pages:** 500 - 502\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 72 retrieves the check digits for the value stored in a specific location within a section of the volatile table. Reference Information: Section 8, “Storing values in the volatile table.”\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<72#Location#[Table Section#]>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<82#Remaining Locations#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 72 |\n| 1 | 🌸 Location (AKB) | 1 - 4 | The location to be verified. When verifying a value from section 0, this field contains a number in the range of 0000 - 0999. When verifying a row of a Diebold Number Table from section 1, this field contains a number in the range of 0000 - 9999. |\n| 1 | 🟪 Location (Variant) | 1 - 4 | The location to be verified. This field contains a number in the range of 0000 - 0999. |\n| 2 | 🌸 [Table Section#] (AKB) | [1] | This field is optional. When present, it specifies the section of the table. This field contains a decimal digit, where: 0 = DES key or conversion table section 1 = Diebold Number Table section When this field is not present, the volatile table section is section 0. |\n| 2 | 🟪 [Table Section#] (Variant) | [0] | This field must not exist |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 82 |\n| 1 | 🌸 Remaining Locations (AKB) | 4 | The number of locations available. This field contains a number in the range of 0000 - 0998. |\n| 1 | 🟪 Remaining Locations (Variant) | 4 | The number of locations available. This field contains a number in the range of 0000 - 9998. |\n| 2 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The key, conversion table, or Diebold Number Table row check digits are the leftmost four hexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros under the key, conversion table, or Diebold Number Table row. If option 88 is enabled, the leftmost six check digits are returned. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n\n#### 🌸 AKB Usage Notes\n\n- The HSM returns an error message <00#0701...> when the specified location is empty.\n- For AKB and Variant key types, the following personality distinctions apply: AKB Examples Verify a DES key in location 17 The command looks like this: <72#17#> The HSM returns this response: <82#1950#D5D4#> Verify a row of a Diebold Number Table in location 438 The command looks like this: <72#438#1#> The HSM returns this response: <82#9950#D5D4#>\n\n#### 🟪 Variant Usage Notes\n\n- 2key-3DES (double-length) keys are loaded in two consecutive locations within the table. When verifying a 2key-3DES (double-length) key, indicate the first of the two locations. For example, if a 2key-3DES (double-length) key is stored in locations 3 and 4, specify location 3 to verify the entire key. Variant Example The command looks like this: <72#17#> The HSM returns this response: <82#1950#D5D4#>\n\n"
    },
