      "es": "# Command 93 - Generate Random Number\n\n- **Command ID:** `93`\n- **Title:** Generate Random Number\n- **PDF Pages:** 523 - 524\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 93 generates a random hexadecimal or decimal number.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<93#[Format#Length#]>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<A3#Random Number#>\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 93 |\n| 1 | [Format#] | 1 | The format of the random number. This field contains an uppercase letter, where: D = decimal H = hexadecimal If this field is empty, the random number is in hexadecimal format. Legal Characters: D, H |\n| 2 | [Length#] | 1 - 3 | The length of the value to generate, 4-512. If this field is empty, the length of the random number is 16 digits. Legal Characters: 0-9 |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | A3 |\n| 1 | 00 | 1 - 512 | The random number. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- Fields one and two are optional, however field 2 cannot exist without field 1. If both fields are omitted, the command generates 16 hexadecimal characters.\n\n### Examples\n\nExamples\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<93#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<A3#A23D79FEDB1329AB#>\n```\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<93#H#4#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<A3#1A7B#>\n```\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<93#D#6#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<A3#327179#>\n```\n\n",
