          "es": "[AKB] The Initialization Vector. This field is ignored and may be empty when field 2 contains 0 . For all other modes, when this field is empty, the HSM generates a random Initialization Vector. This field can be empty only when field 1 (Operation) contains the uppercase letter E . When this field contains the uppercase letter D, the HSM will use binary zeros as the Initialization Vector. When this field contains 16 hexadecimal characters, the HSM will use these digits as the Initialization Vector. When this field contains 74 printable ASCII characters, this field is the Initialization Vector encrypted under the MFK. Headers Supported: 3DES MFK 1IDN*000, where * = E or N. Headers Supported: AES MFK 3IDN*000, where * = E, N, or S. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII | [VARIANT] The Initialization Vector. When this field is empty, the HSM will generate a random Initialization Vector. This field can be empty only when field 1 (Operation) contains the uppercase letter E. When this field contains the uppercase letter D, the HSM will use binary zeros as the Initialization Vector. When this field contains 16 hexadecimal characters, this field is the Initialization Vector encrypted under variant 6 of the MFK. Legal Characters: 0-9, A-F",
