    "source": "Utimaco Atalla AT1000 Command Reference Manual v8.60 (Command 9A)",
    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 9A - AKB Header Mapping\n\n- **Command ID:** `9A`\n- **Title:** AKB Header Mapping\n- **PDF Pages:** 566 - 568\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nThis command accepts an AKB header and returns the corresponding version D header from TR-31.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<9A#AKB2TR31#AKB Header#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<AA#AKB2TR31#[TR-31 Header]#Exportability Status#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 9A |\n| 1 | AKB2TR31 | 8 | AKB2TR31 |\n| 2 | AKB Header | 8 | The AKB Header to map to TR-31 header. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | AA |\n| 1 | AKB2TR31 | 8 | AKB2TR31 |\n| 2 | [TR-31 Header] | 0, 16, 32, 40 | The version D header corresponding to the input header. If the header only has a mapping using the Atalla proprietary block, then that block is included in the header. If response field 3 = 4, then this field will be empty. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n| 3 | Exportability Status | 1 | Indicates if a key with the input header could be exported given the current security settings of the HSM. 0 - Header is exportable. 1 - Header is marked non-exportable. You cannot export a key with this header, but you may be able to generate and export a key with this header. 2 - Header cannot be exported because of option E1 settings. 3 - Header cannot be exported because of the contents of the settings_x.prm file under the AT41_EXPORT key word. The response will not indicate if more than one reason applies. For example, if Option E1 = \"PMD\" and you try to export a key with header 1KDNN000, this command will return '1' indicating the KEK is nonexportable and will not check that the header also fails the E1 test. 4 - Header cannot be exported via TR-31 commands because there is no supported mapping between the AKB header and TR-31. Response field 2 will be empty. Legal Characters: 0-4 |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- Note that the TR-31 header returned in the response will vary from the actual value returned from command 311 in three ways:\n- This command will not include the length of the final key block. Instead, bytes 1-4 of the header will be filled with zeros.\n- This command will not allow the user to specify any optional header blocks.\n- This command will let you know if a key with this header would be exportable given the current configuration of the HSM.\n\n### Examples\n\nExamples\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<9A#AKB2TR31#3PUNE000#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<AA#AKB2TR31#D0000P0TB00E0000#0#>\n```\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<9A#AKB2TR31#1PUNN0I0#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<AA#AKB2TR31#D0000K0TD00N02004112Atalla1PUNN0I0PB0E0000000000#1#>\n```\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<9A#AKB2TR31#3M2NS000#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<AA#AKB2TR31#D0000M7HC00S0200HM0621PB0A000000#>\n```\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 9A - AKB Header Mapping\n\n- **Command ID:** `9A`\n- **Title:** AKB Header Mapping\n- **PDF Pages:** 566 - 568\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nThis command accepts an AKB header and returns the corresponding version D header from TR-31.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<9A#AKB2TR31#AKB Header#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<AA#AKB2TR31#[TR-31 Header]#Exportability Status#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 9A |\n| 1 | AKB2TR31 | 8 | AKB2TR31 |\n| 2 | AKB Header | 8 | The AKB Header to map to TR-31 header. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | AA |\n| 1 | AKB2TR31 | 8 | AKB2TR31 |\n| 2 | [TR-31 Header] | 0, 16, 32, 40 | The version D header corresponding to the input header. If the header only has a mapping using the Atalla proprietary block, then that block is included in the header. If response field 3 = 4, then this field will be empty. Legal Characters: Printable ASCII |\n| 3 | Exportability Status | 1 | Indicates if a key with the input header could be exported given the current security settings of the HSM. 0 - Header is exportable. 1 - Header is marked non-exportable. You cannot export a key with this header, but you may be able to generate and export a key with this header. 2 - Header cannot be exported because of option E1 settings. 3 - Header cannot be exported because of the contents of the settings_x.prm file under the AT41_EXPORT key word. The response will not indicate if more than one reason applies. For example, if Option E1 = \"PMD\" and you try to export a key with header 1KDNN000, this command will return '1' indicating the KEK is nonexportable and will not check that the header also fails the E1 test. 4 - Header cannot be exported via TR-31 commands because there is no supported mapping between the AKB header and TR-31. Response field 2 will be empty. Legal Characters: 0-4 |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- Note that the TR-31 header returned in the response will vary from the actual value returned from command 311 in three ways:\n- This command will not include the length of the final key block. Instead, bytes 1-4 of the header will be filled with zeros.\n- This command will not allow the user to specify any optional header blocks.\n- This command will let you know if a key with this header would be exportable given the current configuration of the HSM.\n\n### Examples\n\nExamples\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<9A#AKB2TR31#3PUNE000#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<AA#AKB2TR31#D0000P0TB00E0000#0#>\n```\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<9A#AKB2TR31#1PUNN0I0#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<AA#AKB2TR31#D0000K0TD00N02004112Atalla1PUNN0I0PB0E0000000000#1#>\n```\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<9A#AKB2TR31#3M2NS000#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<AA#AKB2TR31#D0000M7HC00S0200HM0621PB0A000000#>\n```\n\n"
    },
