    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 9A - HSM Count Status\n\n- **Command ID:** `9A`\n- **Title:** HSM Count Status\n- **PDF Pages:** 573 - 574\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 9A – HSM Count Status returns a list of counted commands and their current count value. CAUTION: Once the counter value reaches zero, the HSM will return an error <00#0300xx#> instead of processing the counted command.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<9A#COUNT#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<AA#Serial Number#0#[Command-Counter#][Command-Counter#] [Command-Counter#][Command-Counter#][Command-Counter#] [Command-Counter#][Command-Counter#][Command-Counter#] [Command-Counter#]>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 9A |\n| 1 | COUNT | 5 | This field contains the word COUNT. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | AA |\n| 1 | HSM Serial Number | 6 | The HSM serial number. This field contains six alphanumeric characters. |\n| 2 | 0 | 1 | This field contains the number 0. |\n| 3 | [Command-Counter#] | Variable | The command being counted followed by the current counter value in decimal. This field is present only if there is at least one command being counted. |\n| 4 | [Command-Counter#] | Variable | The command being counted followed by the current counter value in decimal. This field is present only if there is at least two commands being counted. |\n| 5 | [Command-Counter#] | Variable | The command being counted followed by the current counter value in decimal. This field is present only if there is at least three commands being counted. |\n| 6 | [Command-Counter#] | Variable | The command being counted followed by the current counter value in decimal. This field is present only if there is at least four commands being counted. |\n| 7 | [Command-Counter#] | Variable | The command being counted followed by the current counter value in decimal. This field is present only if there is at least five commands being counted. |\n| 8 | [Command-Counter#] | Variable | The command being counted followed by the current counter value in decimal. This field is present only if there is at least six commands being counted. |\n| 9 | [Command-Counter#] | Variable | The command being counted followed by the current counter value in decimal. This field is present only if there is at least seven commands being counted. |\n| 10 | [Command-Counter#] | Variable | The command being counted followed by the current counter value in decimal. This field is present only if there is at least eight commands being counted. |\n| 11 | [Command-Counter#] | Variable | The command being counted followed by the current counter value in decimal. This field is present only if there is at least nine commands being counted. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- Each time the HSM successfully processes a counted command the counter value is decremented by 1. Commands which result in the HSM returning an error response are not counted.\n- A maximum of nine cryptographic commands can be counted. Utility commands cannot be counted. See section 4 of the Atalla Secure Configuration Assistant-3 User Guide for instructions on how to configure command counting.\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> **CAUTION:** Once the counter value reaches zero, the HSM will return an error <00#0300xx#> instead of processing the counted command.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nHSM serial number: D126XL\n\nCommand 10 counter value: 50\n\nCommand 11 counter value: 40\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<9A#COUNT#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<AA#D126XL#1#0010-0000000050#0011-0000000040#>\n```\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 9A - HSM Count Status\n\n- **Command ID:** `9A`\n- **Title:** HSM Count Status\n- **PDF Pages:** 573 - 574\n\n---\n\n### Description\n\nCommand 9A – HSM Count Status returns a list of counted commands and their current count value. CAUTION: Once the counter value reaches zero, the HSM will return an error <00#0300xx#> instead of processing the counted command.\n\n### Key Management Compatibility\n\n| Key Type | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 🌸 AKB | Enabled | 3DES, AES |\n| 🟪 Variant | Enabled | 3DES |\n\n### Command Syntax\n\n```\n<9A#COUNT#>\n```\n\n### Response Syntax\n\n```\n<AA#Serial Number#0#[Command-Counter#][Command-Counter#] [Command-Counter#][Command-Counter#][Command-Counter#] [Command-Counter#][Command-Counter#][Command-Counter#] [Command-Counter#]>[CRLF]\n```\n\n### Command Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 9A |\n| 1 | COUNT | 5 | This field contains the word COUNT. |\n\n### Response Parameters\n\n| Field | Name | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | AA |\n| 1 | HSM Serial Number | 6 | The HSM serial number. This field contains six alphanumeric characters. |\n| 2 | 0 | 1 | This field contains the number 0. |\n| 3 | [Command-Counter#] | Variable | The command being counted followed by the current counter value in decimal. This field is present only if there is at least one command being counted. |\n| 4 | [Command-Counter#] | Variable | The command being counted followed by the current counter value in decimal. This field is present only if there is at least two commands being counted. |\n| 5 | [Command-Counter#] | Variable | The command being counted followed by the current counter value in decimal. This field is present only if there is at least three commands being counted. |\n| 6 | [Command-Counter#] | Variable | The command being counted followed by the current counter value in decimal. This field is present only if there is at least four commands being counted. |\n| 7 | [Command-Counter#] | Variable | The command being counted followed by the current counter value in decimal. This field is present only if there is at least five commands being counted. |\n| 8 | [Command-Counter#] | Variable | The command being counted followed by the current counter value in decimal. This field is present only if there is at least six commands being counted. |\n| 9 | [Command-Counter#] | Variable | The command being counted followed by the current counter value in decimal. This field is present only if there is at least seven commands being counted. |\n| 10 | [Command-Counter#] | Variable | The command being counted followed by the current counter value in decimal. This field is present only if there is at least eight commands being counted. |\n| 11 | [Command-Counter#] | Variable | The command being counted followed by the current counter value in decimal. This field is present only if there is at least nine commands being counted. |\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n- Each time the HSM successfully processes a counted command the counter value is decremented by 1. Commands which result in the HSM returning an error response are not counted.\n- A maximum of nine cryptographic commands can be counted. Utility commands cannot be counted. See section 4 of the Atalla Secure Configuration Assistant-3 User Guide for instructions on how to configure command counting.\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> **CAUTION:** Once the counter value reaches zero, the HSM will return an error <00#0300xx#> instead of processing the counted command.\n\n### Examples\n\nExample\n\nHSM serial number: D126XL\n\nCommand 10 counter value: 50\n\nCommand 11 counter value: 40\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<9A#COUNT#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<AA#D126XL#1#0010-0000000050#0011-0000000040#>\n```\n\n"
    },
